{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KHybMM1wZUXJLsbgaqQjpz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: '三条 Claims 完整保留，Lead with ''debiasing can hurt'' (50% parameter\n2\t  space, up to 5.9x amplification)。 EC-HTE 作为 principled fix，诊断准则作为 practical decision\n3\t  tool。PPCI 互补性升级至 Contribution #4。 Real data 作为 consistent illustration (pattern\n4\t  consistency, NOT ground-truth benchmark)。 Headline: ''Global correction worsens\n5\t  subgroup CATE bias by 2-3x median; EC-HTE reduces bias to near-zero with 250 expert\n6\t  labels; composition with PPCI achieves 0.005 bias under dual error.'' 审稿周期目标 1R\n7\t  accept 或 minor revision。\n8\t\n9\t  '\n10\timagined_experiments:\n11\t- name: Hierarchical Bayesian EC-HTE on Synthetic Data\n12\t  plan_id: exp-001\n13\t  description: 'HB Dirichlet-prior confusion matrix estimator with partial pooling，\n14\t    full regime sweep (extreme/moderate/homogeneous × n_expert 100-2000 × K=2,4)，\n15\t    与 MLE/Laplace 对比。100 MC runs per config，4-chain NUTS MCMC。\n16\t\n17\t    '\n18\t  expected_results:\n19\t    mcmc_rhat_max: 1.005\n20\t    mcmc_ess_min: 1500\n21\t    mcmc_divergent: 0\n22\t    runtime_min: 70\n23\t    total_mc_runs: 3600\n24\t    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n50: 4-9%\n25\t    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k4_n50_moderate: 6-9%\n26\t    hb_coverage_median: 0.93\n27\t    hb_coverage_min: 0.87\n28\t    hyperprior_sensitivity_k2_variation: <1%\n29\t    hyperprior_sensitivity_k4_variation: ~4-5%\n30\t    singularity_guard_triggers: extreme/n=50 only (2-3 per 100 runs)\n31\t  result_rationale: 'best 档下 MCMC 收敛良好 (R̂<1.01, ESS>200) 因为 4-chain NUTS 提供充分探索，\n32\t    Dirichlet 先验与 multinomial likelihood 共轭性保证后验几何良好。 HB 在 n=50 小样本时优势最大 (4-9% RMSE\n33\t    improvement) 因为 partial pooling 的 James-Stein shrinkage 在信息稀缺时借力最强；n≥500 时 MLE\n34\t    已有足够数据， HB 收敛至 MLE (<0.5% 差异)。coverage median 0.93 而非 0.95 因为 HB 后验 区间基于 MCMC\n35\t    样本，有限 MC 引入的 discretization 导致轻微 undercoverage。 hyperprior sensitivity 在 K=4 时更大\n36\t    (~4-5%) 因为 4 subgroup 的 Dirichlet 浓度参数影响更多自由度，但 coverage 不变说明 point estimate 对先验敏感\n37\t    但区间宽度自适应补偿。\n38\t\n39\t    '\n40\t  tables:\n41\t  - title: HB vs MLE RMSE Comparison (K=2)\n42\t    columns:\n43\t    - regime\n44\t    - n_expert\n45\t    - subgroup\n46\t    - hb_rmse\n47\t    - mle_rmse\n48\t    - improvement_pct\n49\t    rows:\n50\t    - - extreme\n51\t      - 50\n52\t      - z0\n53\t      - 0.095\n54\t      - 0.104\n55\t      - 8.7\n56\t    - - extreme\n57\t      - 50\n58\t      - z1\n59\t      - 0.102\n60\t      - 0.108\n61\t      - 5.6\n62\t    - - extreme\n63\t      - 100\n64\t      - z0\n65\t      - 0.065\n66\t      - 0.066\n67\t      - 1.5\n68\t    - - extreme\n69\t      - 100\n70\t      - z1\n71\t      - 0.068\n72\t      - 0.069\n73\t      - 1.4\n74\t    - - extreme\n75\t      - 250\n76\t      - z0\n77\t      - 0.041\n78\t      - 0.042\n79\t      - 2.4\n80\t    - - extreme\n81\t      - 500\n82\t      - z0\n83\t      - 0.029\n84\t      - 0.029\n85\t      - 0.3\n86\t    - - moderate\n87\t      - 50\n88\t      - z0\n89\t      - 0.088\n90\t      - 0.092\n91\t      - 4.3\n92\t    - - moderate\n93\t      - 100\n94\t      - z0\n95\t      - 0.06\n96\t      - 0.061\n97\t      - 1.6\n98\t  - title: HB vs MLE RMSE Comparison (K=4)\n99\t    columns:\n100\t    - regime\n101\t    - n_expert\n102\t    - subgroup\n103\t    - hb_rmse\n104\t    - mle_rmse\n105\t    - improvement_pct\n106\t    rows:\n107\t    - - extreme\n108\t      - 50\n109\t      - sgC\n110\t      - 0.99\n111\t      - 1.3\n112\t      - 23.8\n113\t    - - moderate\n114\t      - 50\n115\t      - sgC\n116\t      - 0.85\n117\t      - 0.93\n118\t      - 8.6\n119\t    - - moderate\n120\t      - 50\n121\t      - sgB\n122\t      - 0.42\n123\t      - 0.52\n124\t      - 19.2\n125\t    - - extreme\n126\t      - 100\n127\t      - sgC\n128\t      - 0.29\n129\t      - 0.46\n130\t      - 37.0\n131\t    - - extreme\n132\t      - 250\n133\t      - sgC\n134\t      - 0.14\n135\t      - 0.15\n136\t      - 6.7\n137\t  - title: Hyperprior Sensitivity (scale ∈ {0.5, 1.0, 2.0})\n138\t    columns:\n139\t    - K\n140\t    - metric\n141\t    - scale_0.5\n142\t    - scale_1.0\n143\t    - scale_2.0\n144\t    rows:\n145\t    - - 2\n146\t      - rmse_mean\n147\t      - 0.0632\n148\t      - 0.0635\n149\t      - 0.0638\n150\t    - - 4\n151\t      - rmse_mean\n152\t      - 0.182\n153\t      - 0.175\n154\t      - 0.168\n155\t    - - 2\n156\t      - coverage\n157\t      - 0.93\n158\t      - 0.93\n159\t      - 0.93\n160\t    - - 4\n161\t      - coverage\n162\t      - 0.92\n163\t      - 0.93\n164\t      - 0.93\n165\t  figures_description:\n166\t  - HB vs MLE RMSE ratio across n_expert (x-axis log scale), 分 K=2/K=4 和 extreme/moderate\n167\t    四面板\n168\t  analysis: 'HB partial pooling 的核心价值在小样本 (n_expert/K < 50)：shrinkage 将不稳定的 per-subgroup\n169\t    MLE 拉向 pooled estimate，降低 variance。K=4/extreme/n=50 的 singularity guard 触发 (2-3/100\n170\t    runs) 说明此边界条件下 MLE 本身不可靠， HB 的正则化是必要的。4-chain MCMC 相比 2-chain 的 ESS 提升 ~4x 确认\n171\t    多链策略对 posterior geometry exploration 的价值。\n172\t\n173\t    '\n174\t- name: Formal Bias Decomposition Verification\n175\t  plan_id: exp-002\n176\t  description: '解析推导 bias = Δπ × Δτ 的 exact identity，系统参数网格上 MC 验证。 K=2 和 K=4 分别验证。包含\n177\t    ''debiasing can hurt'' proposition 的构造性证明。\n178\t\n179\t    '\n180\t  expected_results:\n181\t    r2_bias_identity_k2: 0.994\n182\t    r2_bias_identity_k4: 0.974\n183\t    tightness_ratio_k2_median: 1.003\n184\t    tightness_ratio_k4_median: 1.023\n185\t    debiasing_hurts_pct: 50\n186\t    debiasing_hurts_threshold_delta_misclass: 0.12\n187\t    max_bias_ratio_k2_extreme: 2.86\n188\t    max_bias_ratio_k4_extreme: 2.41\n189\t    coverage_2se_k2: 0.951\n190\t    coverage_2se_k4: 0.94\n191\t  result_rationale: 'R²=0.994 (K=2) 因为二子群下 bias identity 是 exact (population level)，\n192\t    MC 偏差仅来自有限样本噪声 (N=5000, 100 MC runs)。K=4 的 R²=0.974 稍低 因为 sum-of-products form\n193\t    中 4 个子群的 MC 噪声累积（4 个交叉项 vs K=2 的 1 个）， 但仍然是 identity 而非 bound。tightness ratio\n194\t    ≈1.0 进一步确认这是 exact identity。 debiasing hurts 50% (260/520 non-trivial configs)\n195\t    因为当 naive bias 方向与 global correction 方向同号时 correction 有效，异号时 amplify——对称参数网格下\n196\t    恰好 50%。max_bias_ratio K=2 > K=4 (2.86 vs 2.41) 因为 DIM estimator 下 K=2 的两个子群 error\n197\t    rate 差异最大化（所有 heterogeneity 集中在一个对比）， 而 K=4 将 heterogeneity 分散到多个对比，单个子群的 worst-case\n198\t    amplification 反而降低。 这是 DIM estimator 的特性——CausalForest 行为相反 (exp-011)。\n199\t\n200\t    '\n201\t  tables:\n202\t  - title: Bias Identity R² Verification\n203\t    columns:\n204\t    - K\n205\t    - n_configs\n206\t    - R2\n207\t    - tightness_median\n208\t    - tightness_95pct\n209\t    rows:\n210\t    - - 2\n211\t      - 260\n212\t      - 0.994\n213\t      - 1.003\n214\t      - 1.012\n215\t    - - 4\n216\t      - 260\n217\t      - 0.974\n218\t      - 1.023\n219\t      - 1.068\n220\t  - title: Debiasing Hurts Analysis\n221\t    columns:\n222\t    - K\n223\t    - total_configs\n224\t    - hurts_count\n225\t    - hurts_pct\n226\t    - max_ratio\n227\t    - worst_config\n228\t    rows:\n229\t    - - 2\n230\t      - 260\n231\t      - 130\n232\t      - 50.0\n233\t      - 2.86\n234\t      - Δπ=0.20, Δτ=0.50\n235\t    - - 4\n236\t      - 260\n237\t      - 130\n238\t      - 50.0\n239\t      - 2.41\n240\t      - Δπ=0.20, Δτ=0.50\n241\t  - title: Bias Amplification by Parameter Region\n242\t    columns:\n243\t    - delta_pi\n244\t    - delta_tau\n245\t    - k2_ratio\n246\t    - k4_ratio\n247\t    - direction\n248\t    rows:\n249\t    - - 0.05\n250\t      - 0.1\n251\t      - 1.12\n252\t      - 1.08\n253\t      - global improves\n254\t    - - 0.05\n255\t      - 0.5\n256\t      - 1.45\n257\t      - 1.32\n258\t      - global improves\n259\t    - - 0.15\n260\t      - 0.1\n261\t      - 1.85\n262\t      - 1.62\n263\t      - global hurts\n264\t    - - 0.15\n265\t      - 0.5\n266\t      - 2.52\n267\t      - 2.18\n268\t      - global hurts\n269\t    - - 0.2\n270\t      - 0.5\n271\t      - 2.86\n272\t      - 2.41\n273\t      - global hurts (maximum)\n274\t  figures_description:\n275\t  - Δπ × Δτ heatmap showing bias amplification factor，红色=global hurts, 蓝色=global helps\n276\t  - Analytic prediction vs MC bias scatter plot with R² annotation, K=2 和 K=4 双面板\n277\t  analysis: 'bias identity 的 exact 性质（R²>0.97 for both K）为 Claim 1 提供了最强支撑。 50% hurts\n278\t    rate 是对称参数网格的自然结果，但实际应用中 heterogeneity 方向未知， 因此 50% 是 prior probability of harm——足以证明\n279\t    global correction 不可盲目应用。 K-dependence 的 non-monotonicity (K=2 > K=4 for DIM)\n280\t    是一个需要在论文中 显式讨论的 subtle point，避免审稿人误读为 \"more subgroups → always worse\"。\n281\t\n282\t    '\n283\t- name: Semi-Synthetic CSS Benchmark (TweetEval Sentiment)\n284\t  plan_id: exp-003\n285\t  description: 'TweetEval sentiment (N=45K) 上注入已知 CATE heterogeneity structure， GPT-4.1\n286\t    annotation，K=4 subgroups (text features: has_hashtag × text_length)， 100 MC runs，5\n287\t    methods 对比 (oracle/naive/global/stratified_mle/hb_ec_hte)。\n288\t\n289\t    '\n290\t  expected_results:\n291\t    n_subgroups: 4\n292\t    misclass_rates:\n293\t      S0: 0.05\n294\t      S1: 0.1\n295\t      S2: 0.15\n296\t      S3: 0.25\n297\t    subgroup_sizes:\n298\t      S0: ~38%\n299\t      S1: ~38%\n300\t      S2: ~12%\n301\t      S3: ~12%\n302\t    delta_pi: 0.2\n303\t    debiasing_hurts_confirmed: true\n304\t    mc_runs: 100\n305\t    hb_vs_mle_n100_S3_extreme_rmse_improvement: +60%\n306\t    hb_vs_mle_n100_S3_moderate_rmse_improvement: +24%\n307\t    hb_vs_mle_n250_S3_rmse_improvement: +5-17%\n308\t    hb_vs_mle_n500_convergence: <1.6% difference\n309\t    boundary_condition: n_expert≥100 recommended\n310\t    n50_S3_hb_worse: true\n311\t    n50_S3_hb_degradation: -57% RMSE\n312\t  result_rationale: 'S3 (highest error subgroup, ~12% of data) 是 EC-HTE 的 critical\n313\t    test： n=100 时 HB 大幅优于 MLE (+60%) 因为 S3 仅有 ~12 expert labels (100×0.12)， MLE 的\n314\t    confusion matrix 估计极不稳定，而 HB 从其他 3 个子群借力。 n=50 时 HB 反而 worse (-57%) 因为每子群仅 ~6\n315\t    labels，所有子群的 CM 估计 都不可靠，shrinkage target (pooled estimate) 本身也有大方差——这是 boundary\n316\t    condition (n_expert/K < 25) 的直接体现。Δπ=0.20 落在 best 档 [0.1, 0.2] 上界， 因为 semi-synthetic\n317\t    设定中 text features 提供了真实的 annotation difficulty 变异 (hashtag presence 增加 misclassification\n318\t    ~0.07-0.10)。debiasing hurts 在 S0 (lowest error) 最显著：global correction 对已经几乎正确的子群过度校正。\n319\t\n320\t    '\n321\t  tables:\n322\t  - title: Method Comparison — K=4, Extreme Regime\n323\t    columns:\n324\t    - n_expert\n325\t    - subgroup\n326\t    - oracle_rmse\n327\t    - naive_rmse\n328\t    - global_rmse\n329\t    - mle_rmse\n330\t    - hb_rmse\n331\t    rows:\n332\t    - - 100\n333\t      - S0\n334\t      - 0.025\n335\t      - 0.042\n336\t      - 0.068\n337\t      - 0.055\n338\t      - 0.048\n339\t    - - 100\n340\t      - S1\n341\t      - 0.025\n342\t      - 0.058\n343\t      - 0.052\n344\t      - 0.061\n345\t      - 0.054\n346\t    - - 100\n347\t      - S2\n348\t      - 0.035\n349\t      - 0.085\n350\t      - 0.072\n351\t      - 0.098\n352\t      - 0.075\n353\t    - - 100\n354\t      - S3\n355\t      - 0.04\n356\t      - 0.125\n357\t      - 0.095\n358\t      - 0.28\n359\t      - 0.112\n360\t    - - 250\n361\t      - S3\n362\t      - 0.04\n363\t      - 0.125\n364\t      - 0.095\n365\t      - 0.085\n366\t      - 0.081\n367\t    - - 500\n368\t      - S3\n369\t      - 0.04\n370\t      - 0.125\n371\t      - 0.095\n372\t      - 0.072\n373\t      - 0.071\n374\t  - title: Debiasing Hurts Verification (Global vs Naive |bias|)\n375\t    columns:\n376\t    - subgroup\n377\t    - naive_bias\n378\t    - global_bias\n379\t    - ratio\n380\t    - direction\n381\t    rows:\n382\t    - - S0\n383\t      - 0.008\n384\t      - 0.035\n385\t      - 4.4\n386\t      - global hurts\n387\t    - - S1\n388\t      - 0.025\n389\t      - 0.022\n390\t      - 0.9\n391\t      - global helps slightly\n392\t    - - S2\n393\t      - 0.045\n394\t      - 0.038\n395\t      - 0.8\n396\t      - global helps\n397\t    - - S3\n398\t      - 0.095\n399\t      - 0.065\n400\t      - 0.7\n401\t      - global helps\n402\t  figures_description:\n403\t  - Per-subgroup RMSE across n_expert, 5 methods 分色, S3 单独高亮\n404\t  - 'Debiasing hurts demonstration: S0 的 naive vs global bias bar chart'\n405\t  analysis: 'semi-synthetic 设定的价值在于保留了 real text features 的 annotation difficulty\n406\t    structure (Δπ 来自真实 GPT-4.1 misclassification patterns)，同时 ground-truth CATE 已知。S3\n407\t    是 minority subgroup (12%) with highest error——这是 CSS 场景中的 typical pattern (rare\n408\t    categories harder to classify)。HB 的 sweet spot n=100-250 对应 实际预算中 reasonable expert\n409\t    label investment。boundary condition n<50 的公开 增强 paper credibility。\n410\t\n411\t    '\n412\t- name: Real-Data Case Study (UC Berkeley Hate Speech)\n413\t  plan_id: exp-004\n414\t  description: 'UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech 数据集上的 pattern consistency 分析。 GPT-4.1\n415\t    annotation，platform_group × text_length 定义 4 subgroups， 展示 global vs EC-HTE 产生\n416\t    qualitatively different CATE 分布。\n417\t\n418\t    '\n419\t  expected_results:\n420\t    dataset: UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech\n421\t    n_comments: 2496\n422\t    subgroups:\n423\t      plat0_long: 624\n424\t      plat0_short: 624\n425\t      plat23_long: 624\n426\t      plat23_short: 624\n427\t    delta_pi: 0.117\n428\t    global_FPR: 0.139\n429\t    global_FNR: 0.533\n430\t    misclass_heterogeneity_confirmed: true\n431\t    ec_hte_vs_global_qualitative_difference: true\n432\t    bootstrap_ci_overlap: wide, inconclusive on point estimates\n433\t    avg_abs_bias_naive: 0.21\n434\t    avg_abs_bias_global: 0.273\n435\t    avg_abs_bias_ec_hte: 0.313\n436\t  result_rationale: 'Δπ=0.117 落在 best 档 [0.1, 0.2] 下界附近，因为 text features (platform\n437\t    × length) 提供的 misclassification heterogeneity 是 moderate 的——不如 demographic subgroups\n438\t    那么极端，但足以证明 heterogeneity 是 structural 而非 artifact。 EC-HTE avg |bias| (0.313) 高于\n439\t    global (0.273) 看似 counterintuitive，但在 best 档下 这是可接受的：(1) 高 FNR (53%) 意味着 confusion\n440\t    matrix 严重 asymmetric， correction 的 variance 很大；(2) 无 ground-truth CATE，这些 \"bias\"\n441\t    数值 是相对于 semi-synthetic injected CATEs 的 proxy；(3) best 档的 narrative 将此 framed\n442\t    as \"pattern consistency illustration\" 而非 \"EC-HTE outperforms\"。 核心 deliverable\n443\t    是 Δπ>0.1 在 real data 上的确认，以及 qualitative difference in CATE distributions——审稿人需要看到方法在\n444\t    real data 上产生 non-trivial 差异。\n445\t\n446\t    '\n447\t  tables:\n448\t  - title: Subgroup Misclassification Rates (GPT-4.1)\n449\t    columns:\n450\t    - subgroup\n451\t    - n\n452\t    - misclass_rate\n453\t    - FPR\n454\t    - FNR\n455\t    rows:\n456\t    - - plat0_long\n457\t      - 624\n458\t      - 0.266\n459\t      - 0.08\n460\t      - 0.55\n461\t    - - plat0_short\n462\t      - 624\n463\t      - 0.337\n464\t      - 0.12\n465\t      - 0.62\n466\t    - - plat23_long\n467\t      - 624\n468\t      - 0.303\n469\t      - 0.1\n470\t      - 0.58\n471\t    - - plat23_short\n472\t      - 624\n473\t      - 0.383\n474\t      - 0.18\n475\t      - 0.65\n476\t  - title: CATE Estimate Comparison (bootstrap means)\n477\t    columns:\n478\t    - subgroup\n479\t    - naive_cate\n480\t    - global_cate\n481\t    - ec_hte_cate\n482\t    - ci_width\n483\t    rows:\n484\t    - - plat0_long\n485\t      - 0.15\n486\t      - 0.22\n487\t      - 0.19\n488\t      - 0.35\n489\t    - - plat0_short\n490\t      - 0.08\n491\t      - 0.14\n492\t      - 0.11\n493\t      - 0.38\n494\t    - - plat23_long\n495\t      - 0.21\n496\t      - 0.28\n497\t      - 0.24\n498\t      - 0.32\n499\t    - - plat23_short\n500\t      - 0.12\n501\t      - 0.18\n502\t      - 0.15\n503\t      - 0.4\n504\t  figures_description:\n505\t  - Global vs EC-HTE CATE distribution comparison (4 subgroups, bootstrap violin plots)\n506\t  analysis: 'real data 的角色在 best 档中被精确定位为 \"consistent illustration\"： (1) Δπ=0.117\n507\t    确认 misclassification heterogeneity 在 real data 上存在且 non-trivial； (2) 三种方法产生 qualitatively\n508\t    different CATE distributions； (3) wide bootstrap CIs 诚实地报告了估计的不确定性。 高 FNR (53%)\n509\t    本身是有价值的 finding——说明 LLM 在 hate speech detection 上 系统性 under-classify dehumanization，为\n510\t    EC-HTE 的 practical relevance 提供动机。 审稿人可能 question 为什么 EC-HTE 不 outperform global——response\n511\t    是 \"这正是 Claim 3 diagnostic criterion 的价值：Δπ×Δτ 在此 dataset 上 moderate， full stratified\n512\t    correction 的 variance cost 不完全 justified\"。\n513\t\n514\t    '\n515\t- name: Diagnostic Criterion Validation (Cross-Validated)\n516\t  plan_id: exp-005\n517\t  description: 'Δπ×Δτ product 作为 diagnostic criterion 的 ROC 分析。 必须使用 leave-one-setting-out\n518\t    CV 而非 in-sample AUC。 从 exp-001/003 的所有 experimental settings 中计算 criterion。\n519\t\n520\t    '\n521\t  expected_results:\n522\t    subgroup_level_auc_insample: 0.833\n523\t    subgroup_correlation: 0.86\n524\t    diagnostic_auc_cv: 0.78\n525\t    setting_level_auc_insample: 0.49\n526\t    low_pi_hurt_pct: 84.6\n527\t    high_pi_hurt_pct: 15.4\n528\t    cv_method: leave-one-setting-out\n529\t    optimal_threshold_cv: 0.035\n530\t    sensitivity_at_threshold: 0.82\n531\t    specificity_at_threshold: 0.71\n532\t  result_rationale: 'CV AUC 0.78 落在 best 档 [0.75, 0.85]。in-sample subgroup AUC=0.833\n533\t    降至 CV 0.78 因为 leave-one-setting-out 移除了同一 setting 内子群间的相关性—— 同一 regime 下的子群共享\n534\t    CATE heterogeneity 参数，in-sample 时这是 \"information leak\"。 0.78 的 CV AUC 仍然 strong\n535\t    enough 因为 diagnostic criterion 的实用性 不要求完美分类：false negatives (低 Δπ×Δτ 但 global\n536\t    仍 hurts) 的代价是 unnecessarily using global correction (效率损失但不引入 bias)， 而 false positives\n537\t    的代价是 unnecessarily stratifying (多花 expert labels)。 两种 error 的 asymmetric cost\n538\t    使得 0.78 AUC 在 practical decision-making 中 足够有效。setting-level AUC=0.49 (near random)\n539\t    是因为 setting 内混合了 hurt/help 子群，setting-level prediction 本质上是 ill-defined—— 这恰好支持了\n540\t    subgroup-level diagnostic 的必要性。\n541\t\n542\t    '\n543\t  tables:\n544\t  - title: Diagnostic Criterion ROC Summary\n545\t    columns:\n546\t    - evaluation\n547\t    - AUC\n548\t    - n_settings\n549\t    - n_subgroups\n550\t    - method\n551\t    rows:\n552\t    - - in-sample subgroup\n553\t      - 0.833\n554\t      - 24\n555\t      - 72\n556\t      - logistic regression on Δπ×Δτ\n557\t    - - CV subgroup\n558\t      - 0.78\n559\t      - 24\n560\t      - 72\n561\t      - leave-one-setting-out\n562\t    - - in-sample setting\n563\t      - 0.49\n564\t      - 24\n565\t      - 24\n566\t      - majority vote\n567\t  - title: Threshold Analysis (CV)\n568\t    columns:\n569\t    - threshold\n570\t    - sensitivity\n571\t    - specificity\n572\t    - F1\n573\t    - n_flagged\n574\t    rows:\n575\t    - - 0.02\n576\t      - 0.92\n577\t      - 0.55\n578\t      - 0.68\n579\t      - 42\n580\t    - - 0.035\n581\t      - 0.82\n582\t      - 0.71\n583\t      - 0.76\n584\t      - 35\n585\t    - - 0.05\n586\t      - 0.7\n587\t      - 0.82\n588\t      - 0.76\n589\t      - 28\n590\t    - - 0.075\n591\t      - 0.55\n592\t      - 0.9\n593\t      - 0.68\n594\t      - 20\n595\t  figures_description:\n596\t  - 'ROC curve: in-sample vs CV, with optimal threshold annotated'\n597\t  - 'Scatter plot: Δπ×Δτ product vs actual |bias ratio|, colored by CV fold'\n598\t  analysis: 'diagnostic criterion 从 setting-level 重构为 subgroup-level 预测任务后 AUC 从 0.49\n599\t    跃升至 0.78 (CV)，确认了 best 档的核心假设。 in-sample 到 CV 的 drop (~0.05) 是 moderate 的，说明 criterion\n600\t    的 generalization 合理。optimal threshold 0.035 可直接用于 practical guideline： \"if Δπ×Δτ\n601\t    > 0.035 from pilot data, use EC-HTE; otherwise global correction is safe\"。\n602\t\n603\t    '\n604\t- name: Expert Label Budget Sensitivity\n605\t  plan_id: exp-006\n606\t  description: '系统性 sweep n_expert ∈ {50,100,250,500,1000,2000} × K ∈ {2,4,8} × regime\n607\t    ∈ {extreme,moderate}。 找到 EC-HTE > Global 的 RMSE crossover point。验证 HB partial\n608\t    pooling 在小 n 的价值。\n609\t\n610\t    '\n611\t  expected_results:\n612\t    n_mc: 100\n613\t    total_configs: 36\n614\t    crossover_hb_beats_global:\n615\t      K2_extreme: 250\n616\t      K2_moderate: never (global always better)\n617\t      K4_extreme: 1000\n618\t      K4_moderate: 2000\n619\t      K8_extreme: 1500\n620\t      K8_moderate: never\n621\t    hb_vs_mle_pct_configs_hb_better: 87.5\n622\t    hb_best_improvement_K4_moderate_n50: +42.4% RMSE\n623\t    convergence_threshold: 'n≥1000: HB ≈ MLE <0.5%'\n624\t  result_rationale: 'crossover at K=2/extreme n=250 落在 best 档 [200, 300] 因为 2 subgroups\n625\t    with extreme heterogeneity (Δπ≥0.15) 意味着 per-subgroup CM estimation 只需 ~125 labels/subgroup\n626\t    即可击败 global pooling 的 systematic bias。 K=4/extreme 需要 n=1000 (更高) 因为 4 subgroups\n627\t    分摊 expert budget， per-subgroup labels 仅 ~250——需要更多总量才能让 stratified estimation\n628\t    的 variance 低于 global 的 bias。K=2/moderate \"never crosses\" 因为 moderate heterogeneity\n629\t    (Δπ~0.05) 下 global correction 的 bias 小于 stratified 的 additional variance——这是 diagnostic\n630\t    criterion (Claim 3) 正确预测的情形。 K=8 介于 K=4 和 \"too many subgroups\" 之间，crossover at\n631\t    1500 for extreme 说明 K=8 仍然 feasible 但 cost-prohibitive for most studies。 HB 在\n632\t    87.5% configs 优于 MLE 因为 symmetric DGP 下 partial pooling 几乎 never hurts (worst\n633\t    case: 0.1% worse when all subgroups have identical error)。\n634\t\n635\t    '\n636\t  tables:\n637\t  - title: RMSE Crossover Points (n_expert where EC-HTE < Global)\n638\t    columns:\n639\t    - K\n640\t    - regime\n641\t    - crossover_n\n642\t    - per_subgroup_at_crossover\n643\t    - practical_feasibility\n644\t    rows:\n645\t    - - 2\n646\t      - extreme\n647\t      - 250\n648\t      - 125\n649\t      - feasible\n650\t    - - 2\n651\t      - moderate\n652\t      - ∞\n653\t      - N/A\n654\t      - global always better\n655\t    - - 4\n656\t      - extreme\n657\t      - 1000\n658\t      - 250\n659\t      - feasible but expensive\n660\t    - - 4\n661\t      - moderate\n662\t      - 2000\n663\t      - 500\n664\t      - expensive\n665\t    - - 8\n666\t      - extreme\n667\t      - 1500\n668\t      - 188\n669\t      - expensive\n670\t    - - 8\n671\t      - moderate\n672\t      - ∞\n673\t      - N/A\n674\t      - global always better\n675\t  - title: HB vs MLE Improvement Summary\n676\t    columns:\n677\t    - K\n678\t    - n_expert\n679\t    - configs_hb_better\n680\t    - best_improvement\n681\t    - worst_degradation\n682\t    rows:\n683\t    - - 2\n684\t      - 50\n685\t      - 3/4\n686\t      - +8.7%\n687\t      - -0.2%\n688\t    - - 4\n689\t      - 50\n690\t      - 7/8\n691\t      - +42.4%\n692\t      - -1.1%\n693\t    - - 2\n694\t      - 1000\n695\t      - 2/4\n696\t      - +0.3%\n697\t      - -0.1%\n698\t    - - 4\n699\t      - 1000\n700\t      - 4/8\n701\t      - +0.5%\n702\t      - -0.3%\n703\t  figures_description:\n704\t  - 'Budget crossover curves: RMSE(EC-HTE)/RMSE(Global) vs n_expert, 分 K 和 regime\n705\t    六面板'\n706\t  analysis: 'budget sensitivity 的核心 narrative：EC-HTE 值得投资 IFF (1) diagnostic criterion\n707\t    flags high heterogeneity (extreme regime) AND (2) budget ≥ crossover threshold。\n708\t    这直接连接 Claim 2 (method) 和 Claim 3 (diagnostic)。 Expert Budget Recommendation subsection\n709\t    的数据基础完备。\n710\t\n711\t    '\n712\t- name: PPCI + DSL Baseline Comparison\n713\t  plan_id: exp-007\n714\t  description: '(a) PPCI vs EC-HTE on 4 DGPs (covariate-only, outcome-only, both,\n715\t    none)； (b) per-subgroup DSL baseline；(c) EC-HTE+PPCI composition； (d) pure covariate-error\n716\t    control condition。8 methods × 4 DGPs × 100 MC。\n717\t\n718\t    '\n719\t  expected_results:\n720\t    total_rows: 6912\n721\t    methods: 8\n722\t    dgps:\n723\t    - A_covariate_only\n724\t    - B_outcome_only\n725\t    - C_both_errors\n726\t    - D_no_error\n727\t    mc_runs: 100\n728\t    dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2:\n729\t      ec_hte_ppci_bias_z0: 0.005\n730\t      ec_hte_ppci_rmse_z0: 0.225\n731\t      ec_hte_bias_z0: 0.178\n732\t      ec_hte_rmse_z0: 0.226\n733\t      ppci_bias_z0: 0.004\n734\t      ppci_rmse_z0: 0.261\n735\t      naive_bias_z0: 0.251\n736\t    ec_hte_ppci_bias_reduction_vs_ec_hte: 35x\n737\t    dgp_a_ec_hte_dominates_ppci: true\n738\t    dgp_b_ppci_dominates_ec_hte: true\n739\t    dsl_per_subgroup_vs_ec_hte: EC-HTE wins by 15-25% RMSE via shrinkage\n740\t    coverage_ec_hte_ppci: 1.0\n741\t  result_rationale: 'DGP C (both errors) 中 ec_hte_ppci 的 0.005 bias 落在 best 档 [0.002,\n742\t    0.01] 因为 EC-HTE 和 PPCI 在 composition 中是 necessary and sufficient： EC-HTE 的 M⁻¹\n743\t    correction 消除 structured covariate error (从 0.251 → 0.178)， PPCI 的 residual rectifier\n744\t    消除 remaining outcome error (从 0.178 → 0.005)。 residual 0.005 来自有限样本 MC noise，不是\n745\t    systematic bias。 35x improvement 因为 ec_hte alone 在 DGP C 中仅修正了 covariate-side，\n746\t    outcome-side error (FNR/FPR asymmetry) 贡献了 ~0.17 的 residual bias。 DGP A 中 EC-HTE\n747\t    dominates PPCI 因为 PPCI 的 general-purpose rectifier 不利用 confusion matrix structure——对\n748\t    pure covariate error， structured correction (M⁻¹) 比 nonparametric rectifier 更\n749\t    efficient。 DSL per-subgroup 比 EC-HTE 差 15-25% RMSE 因为缺少 cross-subgroup shrinkage，\n750\t    每个子群独立估计 correction factor，variance 更高。\n751\t\n752\t    '\n753\t  tables:\n754\t  - title: DGP C — Method Comparison (K=2, extreme, n=250)\n755\t    columns:\n756\t    - method\n757\t    - bias_z0\n758\t    - rmse_z0\n759\t    - coverage_z0\n760\t    - bias_z1\n761\t    - rmse_z1\n762\t    rows:\n763\t    - - naive\n764\t      - 0.251\n765\t      - 0.269\n766\t      - 0.82\n767\t      - 0.195\n768\t      - 0.225\n769\t    - - global\n770\t      - 0.185\n771\t      - 0.215\n772\t      - 0.85\n773\t      - 0.142\n774\t      - 0.185\n775\t    - - ec_hte\n776\t      - 0.178\n777\t      - 0.226\n778\t      - 0.92\n779\t      - 0.125\n780\t      - 0.195\n781\t    - - ppci\n782\t      - 0.004\n783\t      - 0.261\n784\t      - 1.0\n785\t      - 0.003\n786\t      - 0.248\n787\t    - - ec_hte_ppci\n788\t      - 0.005\n789\t      - 0.225\n790\t      - 1.0\n791\t      - 0.004\n792\t      - 0.212\n793\t    - - dsl_subgroup\n794\t      - 0.008\n795\t      - 0.275\n796\t      - 0.95\n797\t      - 0.006\n798\t      - 0.26\n799\t  - title: Complementarity Matrix (which method dominates in which DGP)\n800\t    columns:\n801\t    - DGP\n802\t    - best_method\n803\t    - bias\n804\t    - rationale\n805\t    rows:\n806\t    - - A_covariate\n807\t      - ec_hte\n808\t      - 0.008\n809\t      - structured M⁻¹ correction optimal\n810\t    - - B_outcome\n811\t      - ppci\n812\t      - 0.003\n813\t      - rectifier captures outcome error\n814\t    - - C_both\n815\t      - ec_hte_ppci\n816\t      - 0.005\n817\t      - composition covers both error types\n818\t    - - D_none\n819\t      - oracle≈naive\n820\t      - 0.002\n821\t      - no correction needed\n822\t  figures_description:\n823\t  - '4-panel DGP comparison: bias bar chart per method, DGP A-D'\n824\t  - 'EC-HTE + PPCI composition diagram: covariate correction → outcome correction\n825\t    pipeline'\n826\t  analysis: 'complementarity structure 完美支撑 Contribution #4：ec_hte 和 ppci 各自 necessary\n827\t    (单独都不足以处理 dual error)，composition sufficient (bias → near-zero)。 这不是 trivial 的\n828\t    stacking——ec_hte 的 M⁻¹ correction 改变了 PPCI 的 input distribution， 使 rectifier 只需处理\n829\t    residual outcome error 而非混合的 covariate+outcome error。 DSL per-subgroup 作为 baseline\n830\t    展示了 shrinkage 的价值。\n831\t\n832\t    '\n833\t- name: Multiple LLM Annotator Comparison\n834\t  plan_id: exp-008\n835\t  description: 'GPT-3.5-turbo, GPT-4.1, GPT-4o, GPT-4o-mini, GPT-4-turbo, GPT-5.4\n836\t    六个模型 在 TweetEval sentiment 上的 misclassification heterogeneity patterns。 验证 heterogeneity\n837\t    是 structural (跨模型一致) 而非 model-specific artifact。\n838\t\n839\t    '\n840\t  expected_results:\n841\t    models_completed: 6\n842\t    effective_delta_pi:\n843\t      gpt-3.5-turbo: 0.198\n844\t      gpt-4-turbo: 0.149\n845\t      gpt-4.1: 0.098\n846\t      gpt-4o: 0.08\n847\t      gpt-4o-mini: 0.136\n848\t      gpt-5.4: 0.114\n849\t    all_delta_pi_above_005: true\n850\t    multi_llm_delta_pi_min: 0.08\n851\t    worst_subgroup_consensus: True_medium (5/6 models)\n852\t    cross_model_spearman_significant_pairs: 4\n853\t  result_rationale: '所有 6 个模型 Δπ > 0.05 (best 档 min [0.05, 0.08] 的 0.080 落在范围内) 因为\n854\t    misclassification heterogeneity 的 root cause 是 text features (hashtag, length)\n855\t    对 annotation difficulty 的 structural effect——不同模型有不同 overall accuracy， 但 difficulty\n856\t    ranking 相似 (True_medium 最难: 含 hashtag 的中等长度 text 语义歧义最大)。GPT-3.5-turbo Δπ 最高 (0.198)\n857\t    因为 overall accuracy 最低时 per-subgroup variance 也最大；GPT-4o Δπ 最低 (0.080) 因为是最强模型，\n858\t    error rates 被压缩但 heterogeneity 的 relative pattern 仍存。 significant Spearman pairs\n859\t    (4/15) 受限于仅 4 个 subgroups 的 statistical power—— 但 qualitative agreement (5/6 agree\n860\t    on worst subgroup) 提供了 stronger evidence。\n861\t\n862\t    '\n863\t  tables:\n864\t  - title: Cross-Model Misclassification Heterogeneity\n865\t    columns:\n866\t    - model\n867\t    - overall_accuracy\n868\t    - delta_pi\n869\t    - worst_subgroup\n870\t    - best_subgroup\n871\t    rows:\n872\t    - - gpt-3.5-turbo\n873\t      - 0.72\n874\t      - 0.198\n875\t      - True_medium\n876\t      - False_medium\n877\t    - - gpt-4-turbo\n878\t      - 0.81\n879\t      - 0.149\n880\t      - True_medium\n881\t      - False_medium\n882\t    - - gpt-4.1\n883\t      - 0.86\n884\t      - 0.098\n885\t      - True_medium\n886\t      - False_short\n887\t    - - gpt-4o\n888\t      - 0.88\n889\t      - 0.08\n890\t      - True_medium\n891\t      - False_medium\n892\t    - - gpt-4o-mini\n893\t      - 0.83\n894\t      - 0.136\n895\t      - True_medium\n896\t      - False_medium\n897\t    - - gpt-5.4\n898\t      - 0.9\n899\t      - 0.114\n900\t      - True_short\n901\t      - False_medium\n902\t  - title: Per-Subgroup Misclass Rates by Model\n903\t    columns:\n904\t    - model\n905\t    - False_medium\n906\t    - False_short\n907\t    - True_medium\n908\t    - True_short\n909\t    rows:\n910\t    - - gpt-3.5-turbo\n911\t      - 0.12\n912\t      - 0.15\n913\t      - 0.32\n914\t      - 0.25\n915\t    - - gpt-4.1\n916\t      - 0.1\n917\t      - 0.14\n918\t      - 0.2\n919\t      - 0.17\n920\t    - - gpt-4o\n921\t      - 0.08\n922\t      - 0.11\n923\t      - 0.16\n924\t      - 0.14\n925\t    - - gpt-5.4\n926\t      - 0.07\n927\t      - 0.1\n928\t      - 0.18\n929\t      - 0.15\n930\t  figures_description:\n931\t  - Per-subgroup misclass rate profile across 6 models (parallel coordinates plot)\n932\t  analysis: 'multi-LLM evidence 将 paper 的 contribution 从 \"GPT-4.1-specific finding\"\n933\t    提升为 \"structural phenomenon across LLM generations\"。worst_subgroup consensus (True_medium,\n934\t    5/6) 说明 text features 对 annotation difficulty 的 effect 是 robust to model architecture/scale。这直接支持了\n935\t    \"heterogeneity is inherent to the task, not the model\" 的 narrative，strengthening\n936\t    Claim 1 的 practical relevance。 Move to appendix per writing requirements (exp-008/009\n937\t    → appendix)。\n938\t\n939\t    '\n940\t- name: Adaptive Expert Annotation Allocation\n941\t  plan_id: exp-009\n942\t  description: 'CATE-weighted allocation (targeting high-CATE × high-error subgroups)\n943\t    vs uniform allocation vs uncertainty-only allocation。100 MC runs， K=4, extreme\n944\t    regime, n_expert ∈ {100, 250, 500}。\n945\t\n946\t    '\n947\t  expected_results:\n948\t    n_mc: 100\n949\t    K: 4\n950\t    regime: extreme\n951\t    n_expert_grid:\n952\t    - 100\n953\t    - 250\n954\t    - 500\n955\t    allocation_strategies:\n956\t    - uniform\n957\t    - uncertainty_only\n958\t    - cate_weighted\n959\t    rmse_improvement_cate_weighted_vs_uniform:\n960\t      n100: 8-15%\n961\t      n250: 5-10%\n962\t      n500: 2-5%\n963\t    bias_improvement_cate_weighted_vs_uniform:\n964\t      n100: 12-20%\n965\t      n250: 8-12%\n966\t      n500: 3-6%\n967\t    uncertainty_only_vs_uniform: 3-8% RMSE improvement\n968\t    optimal_allocation_fraction_high_error_subgroup: ~2x proportional\n969\t    diminishing_returns_at_n500: true\n970\t  result_rationale: 'CATE-weighted allocation 在 n=100 时改进最大 (8-15% RMSE) 因为 budget\n971\t    最紧张时 将 disproportionate labels 分配给 high-CATE × high-error 子群的 marginal value 最高：\n972\t    这些子群同时具有 (1) 最不稳定的 CM 估计 (high error → high variance) 和 (2) 最高的 CATE bias impact\n973\t    (high CATE → bias 对 final estimate 影响最大)。 n=500 时 diminishing returns (2-5%) 因为所有子群的\n974\t    CM 估计都已 reasonably stable， allocation 优化的 marginal gain 被 Monte Carlo noise 淹没。\n975\t    uncertainty_only (仅 target high error, 不考虑 CATE magnitude) 比 uniform 好但 不如 cate_weighted\n976\t    因为忽略了 CATE heterogeneity——high-error 但 near-zero CATE 的 子群对 overall CATE 估计的影响有限。optimal\n977\t    allocation ~2x proportional 到 high-error subgroup 是 bias-variance tradeoff 的结果：过度分配\n978\t    (>3x) 牺牲了 其他子群的 estimation quality。\n979\t\n980\t    '\n981\t  tables:\n982\t  - title: Allocation Strategy Comparison (K=4, extreme)\n983\t    columns:\n984\t    - n_expert\n985\t    - strategy\n986\t    - mean_rmse\n987\t    - mean_bias\n988\t    - coverage\n989\t    - alloc_sgC\n990\t    rows:\n991\t    - - 100\n992\t      - uniform\n993\t      - 0.185\n994\t      - 0.095\n995\t      - 0.88\n996\t      - 25\n997\t    - - 100\n998\t      - uncertainty\n999\t      - 0.172\n1000\t      - 0.085\n1001\t      - 0.9\n1002\t      - 35\n1003\t    - - 100\n1004\t      - cate_weighted\n1005\t      - 0.16\n1006\t      - 0.078\n1007\t      - 0.91\n1008\t      - 42\n1009\t    - - 250\n1010\t      - uniform\n1011\t      - 0.12\n1012\t      - 0.058\n1013\t      - 0.92\n1014\t      - 62\n1015\t    - - 250\n1016\t      - uncertainty\n1017\t      - 0.112\n1018\t      - 0.052\n1019\t      - 0.93\n1020\t      - 88\n1021\t    - - 250\n1022\t      - cate_weighted\n1023\t      - 0.108\n1024\t      - 0.048\n1025\t      - 0.94\n1026\t      - 105\n1027\t    - - 500\n1028\t      - uniform\n1029\t      - 0.082\n1030\t      - 0.032\n1031\t      - 0.94\n1032\t      - 125\n1033\t    - - 500\n1034\t      - uncertainty\n1035\t      - 0.079\n1036\t      - 0.03\n1037\t      - 0.95\n1038\t      - 175\n1039\t    - - 500\n1040\t      - cate_weighted\n1041\t      - 0.078\n1042\t      - 0.029\n1043\t      - 0.95\n1044\t      - 210\n1045\t  - title: Improvement Summary\n1046\t    columns:\n1047\t    - n_expert\n1048\t    - cate_weighted_vs_uniform_rmse\n1049\t    - cate_weighted_vs_uncertainty_rmse\n1050\t    rows:\n1051\t    - - 100\n1052\t      - +13.5%\n1053\t      - +7.0%\n1054\t    - - 250\n1055\t      - +10.0%\n1056\t      - +3.6%\n1057\t    - - 500\n1058\t      - +4.9%\n1059\t      - +1.3%\n1060\t  figures_description:\n1061\t  - Three allocation strategies' RMSE curves across n_expert, with per-subgroup breakdown\n1062\t  analysis: 'adaptive allocation 是 P2 实验，在 best 档下放入 appendix。其价值在于回应 审稿人可能的 \"how\n1063\t    to optimally spend expert budget\" 问题。CATE-weighted allocation 的 8-15% improvement\n1064\t    at n=100 说明 budget-constrained 场景下 allocation matters，但 n≥500 时差异消失——consistent\n1065\t    with exp-006 的 convergence。 这为 future work 提供了一个 concrete extension point 而不是\n1066\t    current paper 的 core contribution。\n1067\t\n1068\t    '\n1069\t- name: Robustness to Misspecified Subgroup Structure\n1070\t  plan_id: exp-010\n1071\t  description: '测试 EC-HTE 在 subgroup 定义含噪声或 misaligned 时的 graceful degradation。 noise_level\n1072\t    ∈ {0, 0.1, 0.25, 0.5}，K=2 和 K=4。\n1073\t\n1074\t    '\n1075\t  expected_results:\n1076\t    n_mc: 100\n1077\t    noise_levels:\n1078\t    - 0\n1079\t    - 0.1\n1080\t    - 0.25\n1081\t    - 0.5\n1082\t    coverage_hb_range:\n1083\t    - 0.945\n1084\t    - 0.96\n1085\t    coverage_naive_range:\n1086\t    - 0.875\n1087\t    - 0.92\n1088\t    coverage_global_range:\n1089\t    - 0.925\n1090\t    - 0.953\n1091\t    hb_beats_mle_all_configs: true\n1092\t    graceful_convergence_at_50pct: true\n1093\t    hb_improvement_over_mle_range: +0.1% to +0.9% RMSE\n1094\t  result_rationale: 'HB coverage 在所有 noise levels 保持 0.945-0.960 (落在 best 档 [0.92,\n1095\t    0.97]) 因为 partial pooling 的核心机制：当 subgroup labels 含噪声时，per-subgroup CM 估计变差，但\n1096\t    HB 的 shrinkage 自动增加 pooling weight，将估计拉向 global mean—— 效果等同于自适应地从 \"full stratification\"\n1097\t    回退到 \"global correction\"。 noise=0.5 时 HB ≈ Global 因为 50% random label swap 使 subgroup\n1098\t    membership 几乎 uninformative，HB 正确地近乎完全 pool。这是 James-Stein shrinkage 的 经典行为。naive\n1099\t    coverage 低 (87-92%) 因为不做 correction 的 CI 不 account for misclassification error。graceful\n1100\t    degradation 而非 catastrophic failure 直接回应了 Anticipated Reviewer Concern #4。\n1101\t\n1102\t    '\n1103\t  tables:\n1104\t  - title: Coverage Across Noise Levels\n1105\t    columns:\n1106\t    - K\n1107\t    - noise\n1108\t    - coverage_naive\n1109\t    - coverage_global\n1110\t    - coverage_hb\n1111\t    - hb_vs_mle_rmse\n1112\t    rows:\n1113\t    - - 2\n1114\t      - 0.0\n1115\t      - 0.875\n1116\t      - 0.925\n1117\t      - 0.958\n1118\t      - +0.8%\n1119\t    - - 2\n1120\t      - 0.1\n1121\t      - 0.877\n1122\t      - 0.935\n1123\t      - 0.948\n1124\t      - +0.6%\n1125\t    - - 2\n1126\t      - 0.25\n1127\t      - 0.89\n1128\t      - 0.932\n1129\t      - 0.95\n1130\t      - +0.4%\n1131\t    - - 2\n1132\t      - 0.5\n1133\t      - 0.897\n1134\t      - 0.945\n1135\t      - 0.945\n1136\t      - +0.1%\n1137\t    - - 4\n1138\t      - 0.0\n1139\t      - 0.904\n1140\t      - 0.93\n1141\t      - 0.956\n1142\t      - +0.9%\n1143\t    - - 4\n1144\t      - 0.1\n1145\t      - 0.916\n1146\t      - 0.953\n1147\t      - 0.958\n1148\t      - +0.7%\n1149\t    - - 4\n1150\t      - 0.25\n1151\t      - 0.909\n1152\t      - 0.948\n1153\t      - 0.96\n1154\t      - +0.5%\n1155\t    - - 4\n1156\t      - 0.5\n1157\t      - 0.919\n1158\t      - 0.944\n1159\t      - 0.946\n1160\t      - +0.1%\n1161\t  figures_description:\n1162\t  - Coverage vs noise level, 3 methods 分色, K=2/K=4 双面板\n1163\t  analysis: 'coverage 作为 decisive metric (而非 bias 或 RMSE) 的定位在 best 档下特别有效： naive\n1164\t    87-92% = systematically under-covers，EC-HTE 95-96% = near-nominal， global 93-95%\n1165\t    = intermediate。HB 的 graceful degradation 是方法论上的 strong point， 直接回应 \"misspecified\n1166\t    subgroups\" 的审稿人顾虑。\n1167\t\n1168\t    '\n1169\t- name: Causal Forest Integration\n1170\t  plan_id: exp-011\n1171\t  description: 'EC-HTE post-hoc correction on CausalForestDML subgroup CATE estimates。\n1172\t    naive_forest vs global_forest vs ec_hte_forest，100 MC，8 configs。 验证 nonlinear\n1173\t    estimator 下 debiasing-hurts amplification (up to 5.9x for K=4)。\n1174\t\n1175\t    '\n1176\t  expected_results:\n1177\t    n_mc: 100\n1178\t    n_configs: 8\n1179\t    mean_abs_bias:\n1180\t      naive_forest: 0.156\n1181\t      global_forest: 0.107\n1182\t      ec_hte_forest: 0.061\n1183\t    mean_rmse:\n1184\t      naive_forest: 0.178\n1185\t      global_forest: 0.166\n1186\t      ec_hte_forest: 0.229\n1187\t    debiasing_hurts_max_ratio: 5.9\n1188\t    debiasing_hurts_detail: 'K=4/extreme/sg0: global 5.9x worse than naive'\n1189\t    k2_n500_ec_hte_bias_range:\n1190\t    - 0.004\n1191\t    - 0.013\n1192\t    bias_amplification_max_cf: 5.9\n1193\t    ec_hte_bias_reduction_factor_vs_global: 2.6\n1194\t  result_rationale: 'CausalForest 的 5.9x amplification (best 档 [5.0, 6.5]) 显著高于 DIM\n1195\t    的 2.41-2.86x 因为 tree-based estimator 在 subgroup 内部进一步分裂， 每个 leaf 的 CATE 估计噪声在\n1196\t    global correction 时被 heterogeneously amplified。 具体机制：CausalForest 的 honest splitting\n1197\t    将 sample 减半， per-leaf sample size 更小 → CM correction 的 M⁻¹ operation 放大了 leaf-level\n1198\t    estimation noise → subgroup aggregation 时 noise 不 cancel 而 compound。 K=4/extreme\n1199\t    最严重因为 4 个子群中 sg0 (lowest error) 被 global CM 过度校正， 且 forest 的 nonlinear estimation\n1200\t    使得 over-correction 的 propagation 是 multiplicative 而非 additive。ec_hte_forest 的\n1201\t    mean |bias| 0.061 (vs global 0.107) 代表 ~2.6x bias reduction (落在 best 档 [2.0, 4.5])。RMSE\n1202\t    0.229 > global 0.166 体现了 bias-RMSE tradeoff (per-subgroup CM estimation variance\n1203\t    在 forest 上更大)， 这是 Writing Requirement #11 要求 disclose 的。\n1204\t\n1205\t    '\n1206\t  tables:\n1207\t  - title: CausalForest Method Comparison (mean across 8 configs)\n1208\t    columns:\n1209\t    - method\n1210\t    - mean_abs_bias\n1211\t    - mean_rmse\n1212\t    - debiasing_hurts_cases\n1213\t    rows:\n1214\t    - - naive_forest\n1215\t      - 0.156\n1216\t      - 0.178\n1217\t      - —\n1218\t    - - global_forest\n1219\t      - 0.107\n1220\t      - 0.166\n1221\t      - 9\n1222\t    - - ec_hte_forest\n1223\t      - 0.061\n1224\t      - 0.229\n1225\t      - 0\n1226\t  - title: Debiasing Hurts — CausalForest vs DIM\n1227\t    columns:\n1228\t    - estimator\n1229\t    - K\n1230\t    - max_ratio\n1231\t    - worst_config\n1232\t    - mechanism\n1233\t    rows:\n1234\t    - - DIM\n1235\t      - 2\n1236\t      - 2.86\n1237\t      - extreme/sg0\n1238\t      - additive over-correction\n1239\t    - - DIM\n1240\t      - 4\n1241\t      - 2.41\n1242\t      - extreme/sg0\n1243\t      - distributed over-correction\n1244\t    - - CausalForest\n1245\t      - 2\n1246\t      - 3.2\n1247\t      - extreme/sg0\n1248\t      - multiplicative via leaves\n1249\t    - - CausalForest\n1250\t      - 4\n1251\t      - 5.9\n1252\t      - extreme/sg0\n1253\t      - compounding leaf noise\n1254\t  - title: K=2, n_expert=500 — Near-Zero Bias Detail\n1255\t    columns:\n1256\t    - config\n1257\t    - ec_hte_bias\n1258\t    - global_bias\n1259\t    - naive_bias\n1260\t    - reduction_factor\n1261\t    rows:\n1262\t    - - extreme/sg0\n1263\t      - 0.004\n1264\t      - 0.109\n1265\t      - 0.052\n1266\t      - 27.3\n1267\t    - - extreme/sg1\n1268\t      - 0.013\n1269\t      - 0.033\n1270\t      - 0.085\n1271\t      - 2.5\n1272\t    - - moderate/sg0\n1273\t      - 0.008\n1274\t      - 0.045\n1275\t      - 0.028\n1276\t      - 5.6\n1277\t    - - moderate/sg1\n1278\t      - 0.011\n1279\t      - 0.022\n1280\t      - 0.065\n1281\t      - 2.0\n1282\t  figures_description:\n1283\t  - DIM vs CausalForest debiasing-hurts amplification comparison (grouped bar chart)\n1284\t  - ec_hte_forest bias across n_expert, showing convergence to near-zero\n1285\t  analysis: 'CausalForest integration 是 Claim 2 的 critical evidence：paper claims \"CausalForestDML\"\n1286\t    但仅有 DIM results 会被审稿人视为 claim-evidence gap。5.9x amplification strengthens Claim\n1287\t    1 (\"debiasing can hurt even more with nonlinear estimators\")。 bias-RMSE tradeoff\n1288\t    (ec_hte RMSE 38% higher than global) 必须在 paper 中 诚实讨论——defense: (1) bias 是 primary\n1289\t    metric for policy decisions， (2) RMSE 在 n≥500 时 competitive，(3) coverage 仍然 near-nominal。'\n1290\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33779107-04cc-4691-9d8a-87f3f46280c6","uuid":"fd96649e-8bf9-4ec4-b93b-a737d7bde0f7","timestamp":"2026-05-21T13:02:34.136Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520/projects/ec_hte_llm_annotation/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T122454/best/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: '三条 Claims 完整保留，Lead with ''debiasing can hurt'' (50% parameter\n  space, up to 5.9x amplification)。 EC-HTE 作为 principled fix，诊断准则作为 practical decision\n  tool。PPCI 互补性升级至 Contribution #4。 Real data 作为 consistent illustration (pattern\n  consistency, NOT ground-truth benchmark)。 Headline: ''Global correction worsens\n  subgroup CATE bias by 2-3x median; EC-HTE reduces bias to near-zero with 250 expert\n  labels; composition with PPCI achieves 0.005 bias under dual error.'' 审稿周期目标 1R\n  accept 或 minor revision。\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Hierarchical Bayesian EC-HTE on Synthetic Data\n  plan_id: exp-001\n  description: 'HB Dirichlet-prior confusion matrix estimator with partial pooling，\n    full regime sweep (extreme/moderate/homogeneous × n_expert 100-2000 × K=2,4)，\n    与 MLE/Laplace 对比。100 MC runs per config，4-chain NUTS MCMC。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    mcmc_rhat_max: 1.005\n    mcmc_ess_min: 1500\n    mcmc_divergent: 0\n    runtime_min: 70\n    total_mc_runs: 3600\n    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k2_n50: 4-9%\n    hb_vs_mle_rmse_improvement_k4_n50_moderate: 6-9%\n    hb_coverage_median: 0.93\n    hb_coverage_min: 0.87\n    hyperprior_sensitivity_k2_variation: <1%\n    hyperprior_sensitivity_k4_variation: ~4-5%\n    singularity_guard_triggers: extreme/n=50 only (2-3 per 100 runs)\n  result_rationale: 'best 档下 MCMC 收敛良好 (R̂<1.01, ESS>200) 因为 4-chain NUTS 提供充分探索，\n    Dirichlet 先验与 multinomial likelihood 共轭性保证后验几何良好。 HB 在 n=50 小样本时优势最大 (4-9% RMSE\n    improvement) 因为 partial pooling 的 James-Stein shrinkage 在信息稀缺时借力最强；n≥500 时 MLE\n    已有足够数据， HB 收敛至 MLE (<0.5% 差异)。coverage median 0.93 而非 0.95 因为 HB 后验 区间基于 MCMC\n    样本，有限 MC 引入的 discretization 导致轻微 undercoverage。 hyperprior sensitivity 在 K=4 时更大\n    (~4-5%) 因为 4 subgroup 的 Dirichlet 浓度参数影响更多自由度，但 coverage 不变说明 point estimate 对先验敏感\n    但区间宽度自适应补偿。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: HB vs MLE RMSE Comparison (K=2)\n    columns:\n    - regime\n    - n_expert\n    - subgroup\n    - hb_rmse\n    - mle_rmse\n    - improvement_pct\n    rows:\n    - - extreme\n      - 50\n      - z0\n      - 0.095\n      - 0.104\n      - 8.7\n    - - extreme\n      - 50\n      - z1\n      - 0.102\n      - 0.108\n      - 5.6\n    - - extreme\n      - 100\n      - z0\n      - 0.065\n      - 0.066\n      - 1.5\n    - - extreme\n      - 100\n      - z1\n      - 0.068\n      - 0.069\n      - 1.4\n    - - extreme\n      - 250\n      - z0\n      - 0.041\n      - 0.042\n      - 2.4\n    - - extreme\n      - 500\n      - z0\n      - 0.029\n      - 0.029\n      - 0.3\n    - - moderate\n      - 50\n      - z0\n      - 0.088\n      - 0.092\n      - 4.3\n    - - moderate\n      - 100\n      - z0\n      - 0.06\n      - 0.061\n      - 1.6\n  - title: HB vs MLE RMSE Comparison (K=4)\n    columns:\n    - regime\n    - n_expert\n    - subgroup\n    - hb_rmse\n    - mle_rmse\n    - improvement_pct\n    rows:\n    - - extreme\n      - 50\n      - sgC\n      - 0.99\n      - 1.3\n      - 23.8\n    - - moderate\n      - 50\n      - sgC\n      - 0.85\n      - 0.93\n      - 8.6\n    - - moderate\n      - 50\n      - sgB\n      - 0.42\n      - 0.52\n      - 19.2\n    - - extreme\n      - 100\n      - sgC\n      - 0.29\n      - 0.46\n      - 37.0\n    - - extreme\n      - 250\n      - sgC\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.15\n      - 6.7\n  - title: Hyperprior Sensitivity (scale ∈ {0.5, 1.0, 2.0})\n    columns:\n    - K\n    - metric\n    - scale_0.5\n    - scale_1.0\n    - scale_2.0\n    rows:\n    - - 2\n      - rmse_mean\n      - 0.0632\n      - 0.0635\n      - 0.0638\n    - - 4\n      - rmse_mean\n      - 0.182\n      - 0.175\n      - 0.168\n    - - 2\n      - coverage\n      - 0.93\n      - 0.93\n      - 0.93\n    - - 4\n      - coverage\n      - 0.92\n      - 0.93\n      - 0.93\n  figures_description:\n  - HB vs MLE RMSE ratio across n_expert (x-axis log scale), 分 K=2/K=4 和 extreme/moderate\n    四面板\n  analysis: 'HB partial pooling 的核心价值在小样本 (n_expert/K < 50)：shrinkage 将不稳定的 per-subgroup\n    MLE 拉向 pooled estimate，降低 variance。K=4/extreme/n=50 的 singularity guard 触发 (2-3/100\n    runs) 说明此边界条件下 MLE 本身不可靠， HB 的正则化是必要的。4-chain MCMC 相比 2-chain 的 ESS 提升 ~4x 确认\n    多链策略对 posterior geometry exploration 的价值。\n\n    '\n- name: Formal Bias Decomposition Verification\n  plan_id: exp-002\n  description: '解析推导 bias = Δπ × Δτ 的 exact identity，系统参数网格上 MC 验证。 K=2 和 K=4 分别验证。包含\n    ''debiasing can hurt'' proposition 的构造性证明。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    r2_bias_identity_k2: 0.994\n    r2_bias_identity_k4: 0.974\n    tightness_ratio_k2_median: 1.003\n    tightness_ratio_k4_median: 1.023\n    debiasing_hurts_pct: 50\n    debiasing_hurts_threshold_delta_misclass: 0.12\n    max_bias_ratio_k2_extreme: 2.86\n    max_bias_ratio_k4_extreme: 2.41\n    coverage_2se_k2: 0.951\n    coverage_2se_k4: 0.94\n  result_rationale: 'R²=0.994 (K=2) 因为二子群下 bias identity 是 exact (population level)，\n    MC 偏差仅来自有限样本噪声 (N=5000, 100 MC runs)。K=4 的 R²=0.974 稍低 因为 sum-of-products form\n    中 4 个子群的 MC 噪声累积（4 个交叉项 vs K=2 的 1 个）， 但仍然是 identity 而非 bound。tightness ratio\n    ≈1.0 进一步确认这是 exact identity。 debiasing hurts 50% (260/520 non-trivial configs)\n    因为当 naive bias 方向与 global correction 方向同号时 correction 有效，异号时 amplify——对称参数网格下\n    恰好 50%。max_bias_ratio K=2 > K=4 (2.86 vs 2.41) 因为 DIM estimator 下 K=2 的两个子群 error\n    rate 差异最大化（所有 heterogeneity 集中在一个对比）， 而 K=4 将 heterogeneity 分散到多个对比，单个子群的 worst-case\n    amplification 反而降低。 这是 DIM estimator 的特性——CausalForest 行为相反 (exp-011)。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Bias Identity R² Verification\n    columns:\n    - K\n    - n_configs\n    - R2\n    - tightness_median\n    - tightness_95pct\n    rows:\n    - - 2\n      - 260\n      - 0.994\n      - 1.003\n      - 1.012\n    - - 4\n      - 260\n      - 0.974\n      - 1.023\n      - 1.068\n  - title: Debiasing Hurts Analysis\n    columns:\n    - K\n    - total_configs\n    - hurts_count\n    - hurts_pct\n    - max_ratio\n    - worst_config\n    rows:\n    - - 2\n      - 260\n      - 130\n      - 50.0\n      - 2.86\n      - Δπ=0.20, Δτ=0.50\n    - - 4\n      - 260\n      - 130\n      - 50.0\n      - 2.41\n      - Δπ=0.20, Δτ=0.50\n  - title: Bias Amplification by Parameter Region\n    columns:\n    - delta_pi\n    - delta_tau\n    - k2_ratio\n    - k4_ratio\n    - direction\n    rows:\n    - - 0.05\n      - 0.1\n      - 1.12\n      - 1.08\n      - global improves\n    - - 0.05\n      - 0.5\n      - 1.45\n      - 1.32\n      - global improves\n    - - 0.15\n      - 0.1\n      - 1.85\n      - 1.62\n      - global hurts\n    - - 0.15\n      - 0.5\n      - 2.52\n      - 2.18\n      - global hurts\n    - - 0.2\n      - 0.5\n      - 2.86\n      - 2.41\n      - global hurts (maximum)\n  figures_description:\n  - Δπ × Δτ heatmap showing bias amplification factor，红色=global hurts, 蓝色=global helps\n  - Analytic prediction vs MC bias scatter plot with R² annotation, K=2 和 K=4 双面板\n  analysis: 'bias identity 的 exact 性质（R²>0.97 for both K）为 Claim 1 提供了最强支撑。 50% hurts\n    rate 是对称参数网格的自然结果，但实际应用中 heterogeneity 方向未知， 因此 50% 是 prior probability of harm——足以证明\n    global correction 不可盲目应用。 K-dependence 的 non-monotonicity (K=2 > K=4 for DIM)\n    是一个需要在论文中 显式讨论的 subtle point，避免审稿人误读为 \"more subgroups → always worse\"。\n\n    '\n- name: Semi-Synthetic CSS Benchmark (TweetEval Sentiment)\n  plan_id: exp-003\n  description: 'TweetEval sentiment (N=45K) 上注入已知 CATE heterogeneity structure， GPT-4.1\n    annotation，K=4 subgroups (text features: has_hashtag × text_length)， 100 MC runs，5\n    methods 对比 (oracle/naive/global/stratified_mle/hb_ec_hte)。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_subgroups: 4\n    misclass_rates:\n      S0: 0.05\n      S1: 0.1\n      S2: 0.15\n      S3: 0.25\n    subgroup_sizes:\n      S0: ~38%\n      S1: ~38%\n      S2: ~12%\n      S3: ~12%\n    delta_pi: 0.2\n    debiasing_hurts_confirmed: true\n    mc_runs: 100\n    hb_vs_mle_n100_S3_extreme_rmse_improvement: +60%\n    hb_vs_mle_n100_S3_moderate_rmse_improvement: +24%\n    hb_vs_mle_n250_S3_rmse_improvement: +5-17%\n    hb_vs_mle_n500_convergence: <1.6% difference\n    boundary_condition: n_expert≥100 recommended\n    n50_S3_hb_worse: true\n    n50_S3_hb_degradation: -57% RMSE\n  result_rationale: 'S3 (highest error subgroup, ~12% of data) 是 EC-HTE 的 critical\n    test： n=100 时 HB 大幅优于 MLE (+60%) 因为 S3 仅有 ~12 expert labels (100×0.12)， MLE 的\n    confusion matrix 估计极不稳定，而 HB 从其他 3 个子群借力。 n=50 时 HB 反而 worse (-57%) 因为每子群仅 ~6\n    labels，所有子群的 CM 估计 都不可靠，shrinkage target (pooled estimate) 本身也有大方差——这是 boundary\n    condition (n_expert/K < 25) 的直接体现。Δπ=0.20 落在 best 档 [0.1, 0.2] 上界， 因为 semi-synthetic\n    设定中 text features 提供了真实的 annotation difficulty 变异 (hashtag presence 增加 misclassification\n    ~0.07-0.10)。debiasing hurts 在 S0 (lowest error) 最显著：global correction 对已经几乎正确的子群过度校正。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Method Comparison — K=4, Extreme Regime\n    columns:\n    - n_expert\n    - subgroup\n    - oracle_rmse\n    - naive_rmse\n    - global_rmse\n    - mle_rmse\n    - hb_rmse\n    rows:\n    - - 100\n      - S0\n      - 0.025\n      - 0.042\n      - 0.068\n      - 0.055\n      - 0.048\n    - - 100\n      - S1\n      - 0.025\n      - 0.058\n      - 0.052\n      - 0.061\n      - 0.054\n    - - 100\n      - S2\n      - 0.035\n      - 0.085\n      - 0.072\n      - 0.098\n      - 0.075\n    - - 100\n      - S3\n      - 0.04\n      - 0.125\n      - 0.095\n      - 0.28\n      - 0.112\n    - - 250\n      - S3\n      - 0.04\n      - 0.125\n      - 0.095\n      - 0.085\n      - 0.081\n    - - 500\n      - S3\n      - 0.04\n      - 0.125\n      - 0.095\n      - 0.072\n      - 0.071\n  - title: Debiasing Hurts Verification (Global vs Naive |bias|)\n    columns:\n    - subgroup\n    - naive_bias\n    - global_bias\n    - ratio\n    - direction\n    rows:\n    - - S0\n      - 0.008\n      - 0.035\n      - 4.4\n      - global hurts\n    - - S1\n      - 0.025\n      - 0.022\n      - 0.9\n      - global helps slightly\n    - - S2\n      - 0.045\n      - 0.038\n      - 0.8\n      - global helps\n    - - S3\n      - 0.095\n      - 0.065\n      - 0.7\n      - global helps\n  figures_description:\n  - Per-subgroup RMSE across n_expert, 5 methods 分色, S3 单独高亮\n  - 'Debiasing hurts demonstration: S0 的 naive vs global bias bar chart'\n  analysis: 'semi-synthetic 设定的价值在于保留了 real text features 的 annotation difficulty\n    structure (Δπ 来自真实 GPT-4.1 misclassification patterns)，同时 ground-truth CATE 已知。S3\n    是 minority subgroup (12%) with highest error——这是 CSS 场景中的 typical pattern (rare\n    categories harder to classify)。HB 的 sweet spot n=100-250 对应 实际预算中 reasonable expert\n    label investment。boundary condition n<50 的公开 增强 paper credibility。\n\n    '\n- name: Real-Data Case Study (UC Berkeley Hate Speech)\n  plan_id: exp-004\n  description: 'UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech 数据集上的 pattern consistency 分析。 GPT-4.1\n    annotation，platform_group × text_length 定义 4 subgroups， 展示 global vs EC-HTE 产生\n    qualitatively different CATE 分布。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    dataset: UC Berkeley Measuring Hate Speech\n    n_comments: 2496\n    subgroups:\n      plat0_long: 624\n      plat0_short: 624\n      plat23_long: 624\n      plat23_short: 624\n    delta_pi: 0.117\n    global_FPR: 0.139\n    global_FNR: 0.533\n    misclass_heterogeneity_confirmed: true\n    ec_hte_vs_global_qualitative_difference: true\n    bootstrap_ci_overlap: wide, inconclusive on point estimates\n    avg_abs_bias_naive: 0.21\n    avg_abs_bias_global: 0.273\n    avg_abs_bias_ec_hte: 0.313\n  result_rationale: 'Δπ=0.117 落在 best 档 [0.1, 0.2] 下界附近，因为 text features (platform\n    × length) 提供的 misclassification heterogeneity 是 moderate 的——不如 demographic subgroups\n    那么极端，但足以证明 heterogeneity 是 structural 而非 artifact。 EC-HTE avg |bias| (0.313) 高于\n    global (0.273) 看似 counterintuitive，但在 best 档下 这是可接受的：(1) 高 FNR (53%) 意味着 confusion\n    matrix 严重 asymmetric， correction 的 variance 很大；(2) 无 ground-truth CATE，这些 \"bias\"\n    数值 是相对于 semi-synthetic injected CATEs 的 proxy；(3) best 档的 narrative 将此 framed\n    as \"pattern consistency illustration\" 而非 \"EC-HTE outperforms\"。 核心 deliverable\n    是 Δπ>0.1 在 real data 上的确认，以及 qualitative difference in CATE distributions——审稿人需要看到方法在\n    real data 上产生 non-trivial 差异。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Subgroup Misclassification Rates (GPT-4.1)\n    columns:\n    - subgroup\n    - n\n    - misclass_rate\n    - FPR\n    - FNR\n    rows:\n    - - plat0_long\n      - 624\n      - 0.266\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.55\n    - - plat0_short\n      - 624\n      - 0.337\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.62\n    - - plat23_long\n      - 624\n      - 0.303\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.58\n    - - plat23_short\n      - 624\n      - 0.383\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.65\n  - title: CATE Estimate Comparison (bootstrap means)\n    columns:\n    - subgroup\n    - naive_cate\n    - global_cate\n    - ec_hte_cate\n    - ci_width\n    rows:\n    - - plat0_long\n      - 0.15\n      - 0.22\n      - 0.19\n      - 0.35\n    - - plat0_short\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.11\n      - 0.38\n    - - plat23_long\n      - 0.21\n      - 0.28\n      - 0.24\n      - 0.32\n    - - plat23_short\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.15\n      - 0.4\n  figures_description:\n  - Global vs EC-HTE CATE distribution comparison (4 subgroups, bootstrap violin plots)\n  analysis: 'real data 的角色在 best 档中被精确定位为 \"consistent illustration\"： (1) Δπ=0.117\n    确认 misclassification heterogeneity 在 real data 上存在且 non-trivial； (2) 三种方法产生 qualitatively\n    different CATE distributions； (3) wide bootstrap CIs 诚实地报告了估计的不确定性。 高 FNR (53%)\n    本身是有价值的 finding——说明 LLM 在 hate speech detection 上 系统性 under-classify dehumanization，为\n    EC-HTE 的 practical relevance 提供动机。 审稿人可能 question 为什么 EC-HTE 不 outperform global——response\n    是 \"这正是 Claim 3 diagnostic criterion 的价值：Δπ×Δτ 在此 dataset 上 moderate， full stratified\n    correction 的 variance cost 不完全 justified\"。\n\n    '\n- name: Diagnostic Criterion Validation (Cross-Validated)\n  plan_id: exp-005\n  description: 'Δπ×Δτ product 作为 diagnostic criterion 的 ROC 分析。 必须使用 leave-one-setting-out\n    CV 而非 in-sample AUC。 从 exp-001/003 的所有 experimental settings 中计算 criterion。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    subgroup_level_auc_insample: 0.833\n    subgroup_correlation: 0.86\n    diagnostic_auc_cv: 0.78\n    setting_level_auc_insample: 0.49\n    low_pi_hurt_pct: 84.6\n    high_pi_hurt_pct: 15.4\n    cv_method: leave-one-setting-out\n    optimal_threshold_cv: 0.035\n    sensitivity_at_threshold: 0.82\n    specificity_at_threshold: 0.71\n  result_rationale: 'CV AUC 0.78 落在 best 档 [0.75, 0.85]。in-sample subgroup AUC=0.833\n    降至 CV 0.78 因为 leave-one-setting-out 移除了同一 setting 内子群间的相关性—— 同一 regime 下的子群共享\n    CATE heterogeneity 参数，in-sample 时这是 \"information leak\"。 0.78 的 CV AUC 仍然 strong\n    enough 因为 diagnostic criterion 的实用性 不要求完美分类：false negatives (低 Δπ×Δτ 但 global\n    仍 hurts) 的代价是 unnecessarily using global correction (效率损失但不引入 bias)， 而 false positives\n    的代价是 unnecessarily stratifying (多花 expert labels)。 两种 error 的 asymmetric cost\n    使得 0.78 AUC 在 practical decision-making 中 足够有效。setting-level AUC=0.49 (near random)\n    是因为 setting 内混合了 hurt/help 子群，setting-level prediction 本质上是 ill-defined—— 这恰好支持了\n    subgroup-level diagnostic 的必要性。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Diagnostic Criterion ROC Summary\n    columns:\n    - evaluation\n    - AUC\n    - n_settings\n    - n_subgroups\n    - method\n    rows:\n    - - in-sample subgroup\n      - 0.833\n      - 24\n      - 72\n      - logistic regression on Δπ×Δτ\n    - - CV subgroup\n      - 0.78\n      - 24\n      - 72\n      - leave-one-setting-out\n    - - in-sample setting\n      - 0.49\n      - 24\n      - 24\n      - majority vote\n  - title: Threshold Analysis (CV)\n    columns:\n    - threshold\n    - sensitivity\n    - specificity\n    - F1\n    - n_flagged\n    rows:\n    - - 0.02\n      - 0.92\n      - 0.55\n      - 0.68\n      - 42\n    - - 0.035\n      - 0.82\n      - 0.71\n      - 0.76\n      - 35\n    - - 0.05\n      - 0.7\n      - 0.82\n      - 0.76\n      - 28\n    - - 0.075\n      - 0.55\n      - 0.9\n      - 0.68\n      - 20\n  figures_description:\n  - 'ROC curve: in-sample vs CV, with optimal threshold annotated'\n  - 'Scatter plot: Δπ×Δτ product vs actual |bias ratio|, colored by CV fold'\n  analysis: 'diagnostic criterion 从 setting-level 重构为 subgroup-level 预测任务后 AUC 从 0.49\n    跃升至 0.78 (CV)，确认了 best 档的核心假设。 in-sample 到 CV 的 drop (~0.05) 是 moderate 的，说明 criterion\n    的 generalization 合理。optimal threshold 0.035 可直接用于 practical guideline： \"if Δπ×Δτ\n    > 0.035 from pilot data, use EC-HTE; otherwise global correction is safe\"。\n\n    '\n- name: Expert Label Budget Sensitivity\n  plan_id: exp-006\n  description: '系统性 sweep n_expert ∈ {50,100,250,500,1000,2000} × K ∈ {2,4,8} × regime\n    ∈ {extreme,moderate}。 找到 EC-HTE > Global 的 RMSE crossover point。验证 HB partial\n    pooling 在小 n 的价值。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_mc: 100\n    total_configs: 36\n    crossover_hb_beats_global:\n      K2_extreme: 250\n      K2_moderate: never (global always better)\n      K4_extreme: 1000\n      K4_moderate: 2000\n      K8_extreme: 1500\n      K8_moderate: never\n    hb_vs_mle_pct_configs_hb_better: 87.5\n    hb_best_improvement_K4_moderate_n50: +42.4% RMSE\n    convergence_threshold: 'n≥1000: HB ≈ MLE <0.5%'\n  result_rationale: 'crossover at K=2/extreme n=250 落在 best 档 [200, 300] 因为 2 subgroups\n    with extreme heterogeneity (Δπ≥0.15) 意味着 per-subgroup CM estimation 只需 ~125 labels/subgroup\n    即可击败 global pooling 的 systematic bias。 K=4/extreme 需要 n=1000 (更高) 因为 4 subgroups\n    分摊 expert budget， per-subgroup labels 仅 ~250——需要更多总量才能让 stratified estimation\n    的 variance 低于 global 的 bias。K=2/moderate \"never crosses\" 因为 moderate heterogeneity\n    (Δπ~0.05) 下 global correction 的 bias 小于 stratified 的 additional variance——这是 diagnostic\n    criterion (Claim 3) 正确预测的情形。 K=8 介于 K=4 和 \"too many subgroups\" 之间，crossover at\n    1500 for extreme 说明 K=8 仍然 feasible 但 cost-prohibitive for most studies。 HB 在\n    87.5% configs 优于 MLE 因为 symmetric DGP 下 partial pooling 几乎 never hurts (worst\n    case: 0.1% worse when all subgroups have identical error)。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: RMSE Crossover Points (n_expert where EC-HTE < Global)\n    columns:\n    - K\n    - regime\n    - crossover_n\n    - per_subgroup_at_crossover\n    - practical_feasibility\n    rows:\n    - - 2\n      - extreme\n      - 250\n      - 125\n      - feasible\n    - - 2\n      - moderate\n      - ∞\n      - N/A\n      - global always better\n    - - 4\n      - extreme\n      - 1000\n      - 250\n      - feasible but expensive\n    - - 4\n      - moderate\n      - 2000\n      - 500\n      - expensive\n    - - 8\n      - extreme\n      - 1500\n      - 188\n      - expensive\n    - - 8\n      - moderate\n      - ∞\n      - N/A\n      - global always better\n  - title: HB vs MLE Improvement Summary\n    columns:\n    - K\n    - n_expert\n    - configs_hb_better\n    - best_improvement\n    - worst_degradation\n    rows:\n    - - 2\n      - 50\n      - 3/4\n      - +8.7%\n      - -0.2%\n    - - 4\n      - 50\n      - 7/8\n      - +42.4%\n      - -1.1%\n    - - 2\n      - 1000\n      - 2/4\n      - +0.3%\n      - -0.1%\n    - - 4\n      - 1000\n      - 4/8\n      - +0.5%\n      - -0.3%\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Budget crossover curves: RMSE(EC-HTE)/RMSE(Global) vs n_expert, 分 K 和 regime\n    六面板'\n  analysis: 'budget sensitivity 的核心 narrative：EC-HTE 值得投资 IFF (1) diagnostic criterion\n    flags high heterogeneity (extreme regime) AND (2) budget ≥ crossover threshold。\n    这直接连接 Claim 2 (method) 和 Claim 3 (diagnostic)。 Expert Budget Recommendation subsection\n    的数据基础完备。\n\n    '\n- name: PPCI + DSL Baseline Comparison\n  plan_id: exp-007\n  description: '(a) PPCI vs EC-HTE on 4 DGPs (covariate-only, outcome-only, both,\n    none)； (b) per-subgroup DSL baseline；(c) EC-HTE+PPCI composition； (d) pure covariate-error\n    control condition。8 methods × 4 DGPs × 100 MC。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    total_rows: 6912\n    methods: 8\n    dgps:\n    - A_covariate_only\n    - B_outcome_only\n    - C_both_errors\n    - D_no_error\n    mc_runs: 100\n    dgp_c_extreme_n250_k2:\n      ec_hte_ppci_bias_z0: 0.005\n      ec_hte_ppci_rmse_z0: 0.225\n      ec_hte_bias_z0: 0.178\n      ec_hte_rmse_z0: 0.226\n      ppci_bias_z0: 0.004\n      ppci_rmse_z0: 0.261\n      naive_bias_z0: 0.251\n    ec_hte_ppci_bias_reduction_vs_ec_hte: 35x\n    dgp_a_ec_hte_dominates_ppci: true\n    dgp_b_ppci_dominates_ec_hte: true\n    dsl_per_subgroup_vs_ec_hte: EC-HTE wins by 15-25% RMSE via shrinkage\n    coverage_ec_hte_ppci: 1.0\n  result_rationale: 'DGP C (both errors) 中 ec_hte_ppci 的 0.005 bias 落在 best 档 [0.002,\n    0.01] 因为 EC-HTE 和 PPCI 在 composition 中是 necessary and sufficient： EC-HTE 的 M⁻¹\n    correction 消除 structured covariate error (从 0.251 → 0.178)， PPCI 的 residual rectifier\n    消除 remaining outcome error (从 0.178 → 0.005)。 residual 0.005 来自有限样本 MC noise，不是\n    systematic bias。 35x improvement 因为 ec_hte alone 在 DGP C 中仅修正了 covariate-side，\n    outcome-side error (FNR/FPR asymmetry) 贡献了 ~0.17 的 residual bias。 DGP A 中 EC-HTE\n    dominates PPCI 因为 PPCI 的 general-purpose rectifier 不利用 confusion matrix structure——对\n    pure covariate error， structured correction (M⁻¹) 比 nonparametric rectifier 更\n    efficient。 DSL per-subgroup 比 EC-HTE 差 15-25% RMSE 因为缺少 cross-subgroup shrinkage，\n    每个子群独立估计 correction factor，variance 更高。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: DGP C — Method Comparison (K=2, extreme, n=250)\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - bias_z0\n    - rmse_z0\n    - coverage_z0\n    - bias_z1\n    - rmse_z1\n    rows:\n    - - naive\n      - 0.251\n      - 0.269\n      - 0.82\n      - 0.195\n      - 0.225\n    - - global\n      - 0.185\n      - 0.215\n      - 0.85\n      - 0.142\n      - 0.185\n    - - ec_hte\n      - 0.178\n      - 0.226\n      - 0.92\n      - 0.125\n      - 0.195\n    - - ppci\n      - 0.004\n      - 0.261\n      - 1.0\n      - 0.003\n      - 0.248\n    - - ec_hte_ppci\n      - 0.005\n      - 0.225\n      - 1.0\n      - 0.004\n      - 0.212\n    - - dsl_subgroup\n      - 0.008\n      - 0.275\n      - 0.95\n      - 0.006\n      - 0.26\n  - title: Complementarity Matrix (which method dominates in which DGP)\n    columns:\n    - DGP\n    - best_method\n    - bias\n    - rationale\n    rows:\n    - - A_covariate\n      - ec_hte\n      - 0.008\n      - structured M⁻¹ correction optimal\n    - - B_outcome\n      - ppci\n      - 0.003\n      - rectifier captures outcome error\n    - - C_both\n      - ec_hte_ppci\n      - 0.005\n      - composition covers both error types\n    - - D_none\n      - oracle≈naive\n      - 0.002\n      - no correction needed\n  figures_description:\n  - '4-panel DGP comparison: bias bar chart per method, DGP A-D'\n  - 'EC-HTE + PPCI composition diagram: covariate correction → outcome correction\n    pipeline'\n  analysis: 'complementarity structure 完美支撑 Contribution #4：ec_hte 和 ppci 各自 necessary\n    (单独都不足以处理 dual error)，composition sufficient (bias → near-zero)。 这不是 trivial 的\n    stacking——ec_hte 的 M⁻¹ correction 改变了 PPCI 的 input distribution， 使 rectifier 只需处理\n    residual outcome error 而非混合的 covariate+outcome error。 DSL per-subgroup 作为 baseline\n    展示了 shrinkage 的价值。\n\n    '\n- name: Multiple LLM Annotator Comparison\n  plan_id: exp-008\n  description: 'GPT-3.5-turbo, GPT-4.1, GPT-4o, GPT-4o-mini, GPT-4-turbo, GPT-5.4\n    六个模型 在 TweetEval sentiment 上的 misclassification heterogeneity patterns。 验证 heterogeneity\n    是 structural (跨模型一致) 而非 model-specific artifact。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    models_completed: 6\n    effective_delta_pi:\n      gpt-3.5-turbo: 0.198\n      gpt-4-turbo: 0.149\n      gpt-4.1: 0.098\n      gpt-4o: 0.08\n      gpt-4o-mini: 0.136\n      gpt-5.4: 0.114\n    all_delta_pi_above_005: true\n    multi_llm_delta_pi_min: 0.08\n    worst_subgroup_consensus: True_medium (5/6 models)\n    cross_model_spearman_significant_pairs: 4\n  result_rationale: '所有 6 个模型 Δπ > 0.05 (best 档 min [0.05, 0.08] 的 0.080 落在范围内) 因为\n    misclassification heterogeneity 的 root cause 是 text features (hashtag, length)\n    对 annotation difficulty 的 structural effect——不同模型有不同 overall accuracy， 但 difficulty\n    ranking 相似 (True_medium 最难: 含 hashtag 的中等长度 text 语义歧义最大)。GPT-3.5-turbo Δπ 最高 (0.198)\n    因为 overall accuracy 最低时 per-subgroup variance 也最大；GPT-4o Δπ 最低 (0.080) 因为是最强模型，\n    error rates 被压缩但 heterogeneity 的 relative pattern 仍存。 significant Spearman pairs\n    (4/15) 受限于仅 4 个 subgroups 的 statistical power—— 但 qualitative agreement (5/6 agree\n    on worst subgroup) 提供了 stronger evidence。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Cross-Model Misclassification Heterogeneity\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - overall_accuracy\n    - delta_pi\n    - worst_subgroup\n    - best_subgroup\n    rows:\n    - - gpt-3.5-turbo\n      - 0.72\n      - 0.198\n      - True_medium\n      - False_medium\n    - - gpt-4-turbo\n      - 0.81\n      - 0.149\n      - True_medium\n      - False_medium\n    - - gpt-4.1\n      - 0.86\n      - 0.098\n      - True_medium\n      - False_short\n    - - gpt-4o\n      - 0.88\n      - 0.08\n      - True_medium\n      - False_medium\n    - - gpt-4o-mini\n      - 0.83\n      - 0.136\n      - True_medium\n      - False_medium\n    - - gpt-5.4\n      - 0.9\n      - 0.114\n      - True_short\n      - False_medium\n  - title: Per-Subgroup Misclass Rates by Model\n    columns:\n    - model\n    - False_medium\n    - False_short\n    - True_medium\n    - True_short\n    rows:\n    - - gpt-3.5-turbo\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.15\n      - 0.32\n      - 0.25\n    - - gpt-4.1\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.14\n      - 0.2\n      - 0.17\n    - - gpt-4o\n      - 0.08\n      - 0.11\n      - 0.16\n      - 0.14\n    - - gpt-5.4\n      - 0.07\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.18\n      - 0.15\n  figures_description:\n  - Per-subgroup misclass rate profile across 6 models (parallel coordinates plot)\n  analysis: 'multi-LLM evidence 将 paper 的 contribution 从 \"GPT-4.1-specific finding\"\n    提升为 \"structural phenomenon across LLM generations\"。worst_subgroup consensus (True_medium,\n    5/6) 说明 text features 对 annotation difficulty 的 effect 是 robust to model architecture/scale。这直接支持了\n    \"heterogeneity is inherent to the task, not the model\" 的 narrative，strengthening\n    Claim 1 的 practical relevance。 Move to appendix per writing requirements (exp-008/009\n    → appendix)。\n\n    '\n- name: Adaptive Expert Annotation Allocation\n  plan_id: exp-009\n  description: 'CATE-weighted allocation (targeting high-CATE × high-error subgroups)\n    vs uniform allocation vs uncertainty-only allocation。100 MC runs， K=4, extreme\n    regime, n_expert ∈ {100, 250, 500}。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_mc: 100\n    K: 4\n    regime: extreme\n    n_expert_grid:\n    - 100\n    - 250\n    - 500\n    allocation_strategies:\n    - uniform\n    - uncertainty_only\n    - cate_weighted\n    rmse_improvement_cate_weighted_vs_uniform:\n      n100: 8-15%\n      n250: 5-10%\n      n500: 2-5%\n    bias_improvement_cate_weighted_vs_uniform:\n      n100: 12-20%\n      n250: 8-12%\n      n500: 3-6%\n    uncertainty_only_vs_uniform: 3-8% RMSE improvement\n    optimal_allocation_fraction_high_error_subgroup: ~2x proportional\n    diminishing_returns_at_n500: true\n  result_rationale: 'CATE-weighted allocation 在 n=100 时改进最大 (8-15% RMSE) 因为 budget\n    最紧张时 将 disproportionate labels 分配给 high-CATE × high-error 子群的 marginal value 最高：\n    这些子群同时具有 (1) 最不稳定的 CM 估计 (high error → high variance) 和 (2) 最高的 CATE bias impact\n    (high CATE → bias 对 final estimate 影响最大)。 n=500 时 diminishing returns (2-5%) 因为所有子群的\n    CM 估计都已 reasonably stable， allocation 优化的 marginal gain 被 Monte Carlo noise 淹没。\n    uncertainty_only (仅 target high error, 不考虑 CATE magnitude) 比 uniform 好但 不如 cate_weighted\n    因为忽略了 CATE heterogeneity——high-error 但 near-zero CATE 的 子群对 overall CATE 估计的影响有限。optimal\n    allocation ~2x proportional 到 high-error subgroup 是 bias-variance tradeoff 的结果：过度分配\n    (>3x) 牺牲了 其他子群的 estimation quality。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Allocation Strategy Comparison (K=4, extreme)\n    columns:\n    - n_expert\n    - strategy\n    - mean_rmse\n    - mean_bias\n    - coverage\n    - alloc_sgC\n    rows:\n    - - 100\n      - uniform\n      - 0.185\n      - 0.095\n      - 0.88\n      - 25\n    - - 100\n      - uncertainty\n      - 0.172\n      - 0.085\n      - 0.9\n      - 35\n    - - 100\n      - cate_weighted\n      - 0.16\n      - 0.078\n      - 0.91\n      - 42\n    - - 250\n      - uniform\n      - 0.12\n      - 0.058\n      - 0.92\n      - 62\n    - - 250\n      - uncertainty\n      - 0.112\n      - 0.052\n      - 0.93\n      - 88\n    - - 250\n      - cate_weighted\n      - 0.108\n      - 0.048\n      - 0.94\n      - 105\n    - - 500\n      - uniform\n      - 0.082\n      - 0.032\n      - 0.94\n      - 125\n    - - 500\n      - uncertainty\n      - 0.079\n      - 0.03\n      - 0.95\n      - 175\n    - - 500\n      - cate_weighted\n      - 0.078\n      - 0.029\n      - 0.95\n      - 210\n  - title: Improvement Summary\n    columns:\n    - n_expert\n    - cate_weighted_vs_uniform_rmse\n    - cate_weighted_vs_uncertainty_rmse\n    rows:\n    - - 100\n      - +13.5%\n      - +7.0%\n    - - 250\n      - +10.0%\n      - +3.6%\n    - - 500\n      - +4.9%\n      - +1.3%\n  figures_description:\n  - Three allocation strategies' RMSE curves across n_expert, with per-subgroup breakdown\n  analysis: 'adaptive allocation 是 P2 实验，在 best 档下放入 appendix。其价值在于回应 审稿人可能的 \"how\n    to optimally spend expert budget\" 问题。CATE-weighted allocation 的 8-15% improvement\n    at n=100 说明 budget-constrained 场景下 allocation matters，但 n≥500 时差异消失——consistent\n    with exp-006 的 convergence。 这为 future work 提供了一个 concrete extension point 而不是\n    current paper 的 core contribution。\n\n    '\n- name: Robustness to Misspecified Subgroup Structure\n  plan_id: exp-010\n  description: '测试 EC-HTE 在 subgroup 定义含噪声或 misaligned 时的 graceful degradation。 noise_level\n    ∈ {0, 0.1, 0.25, 0.5}，K=2 和 K=4。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_mc: 100\n    noise_levels:\n    - 0\n    - 0.1\n    - 0.25\n    - 0.5\n    coverage_hb_range:\n    - 0.945\n    - 0.96\n    coverage_naive_range:\n    - 0.875\n    - 0.92\n    coverage_global_range:\n    - 0.925\n    - 0.953\n    hb_beats_mle_all_configs: true\n    graceful_convergence_at_50pct: true\n    hb_improvement_over_mle_range: +0.1% to +0.9% RMSE\n  result_rationale: 'HB coverage 在所有 noise levels 保持 0.945-0.960 (落在 best 档 [0.92,\n    0.97]) 因为 partial pooling 的核心机制：当 subgroup labels 含噪声时，per-subgroup CM 估计变差，但\n    HB 的 shrinkage 自动增加 pooling weight，将估计拉向 global mean—— 效果等同于自适应地从 \"full stratification\"\n    回退到 \"global correction\"。 noise=0.5 时 HB ≈ Global 因为 50% random label swap 使 subgroup\n    membership 几乎 uninformative，HB 正确地近乎完全 pool。这是 James-Stein shrinkage 的 经典行为。naive\n    coverage 低 (87-92%) 因为不做 correction 的 CI 不 account for misclassification error。graceful\n    degradation 而非 catastrophic failure 直接回应了 Anticipated Reviewer Concern #4。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: Coverage Across Noise Levels\n    columns:\n    - K\n    - noise\n    - coverage_naive\n    - coverage_global\n    - coverage_hb\n    - hb_vs_mle_rmse\n    rows:\n    - - 2\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.875\n      - 0.925\n      - 0.958\n      - +0.8%\n    - - 2\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.877\n      - 0.935\n      - 0.948\n      - +0.6%\n    - - 2\n      - 0.25\n      - 0.89\n      - 0.932\n      - 0.95\n      - +0.4%\n    - - 2\n      - 0.5\n      - 0.897\n      - 0.945\n      - 0.945\n      - +0.1%\n    - - 4\n      - 0.0\n      - 0.904\n      - 0.93\n      - 0.956\n      - +0.9%\n    - - 4\n      - 0.1\n      - 0.916\n      - 0.953\n      - 0.958\n      - +0.7%\n    - - 4\n      - 0.25\n      - 0.909\n      - 0.948\n      - 0.96\n      - +0.5%\n    - - 4\n      - 0.5\n      - 0.919\n      - 0.944\n      - 0.946\n      - +0.1%\n  figures_description:\n  - Coverage vs noise level, 3 methods 分色, K=2/K=4 双面板\n  analysis: 'coverage 作为 decisive metric (而非 bias 或 RMSE) 的定位在 best 档下特别有效： naive\n    87-92% = systematically under-covers，EC-HTE 95-96% = near-nominal， global 93-95%\n    = intermediate。HB 的 graceful degradation 是方法论上的 strong point， 直接回应 \"misspecified\n    subgroups\" 的审稿人顾虑。\n\n    '\n- name: Causal Forest Integration\n  plan_id: exp-011\n  description: 'EC-HTE post-hoc correction on CausalForestDML subgroup CATE estimates。\n    naive_forest vs global_forest vs ec_hte_forest，100 MC，8 configs。 验证 nonlinear\n    estimator 下 debiasing-hurts amplification (up to 5.9x for K=4)。\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    n_mc: 100\n    n_configs: 8\n    mean_abs_bias:\n      naive_forest: 0.156\n      global_forest: 0.107\n      ec_hte_forest: 0.061\n    mean_rmse:\n      naive_forest: 0.178\n      global_forest: 0.166\n      ec_hte_forest: 0.229\n    debiasing_hurts_max_ratio: 5.9\n    debiasing_hurts_detail: 'K=4/extreme/sg0: global 5.9x worse than naive'\n    k2_n500_ec_hte_bias_range:\n    - 0.004\n    - 0.013\n    bias_amplification_max_cf: 5.9\n    ec_hte_bias_reduction_factor_vs_global: 2.6\n  result_rationale: 'CausalForest 的 5.9x amplification (best 档 [5.0, 6.5]) 显著高于 DIM\n    的 2.41-2.86x 因为 tree-based estimator 在 subgroup 内部进一步分裂， 每个 leaf 的 CATE 估计噪声在\n    global correction 时被 heterogeneously amplified。 具体机制：CausalForest 的 honest splitting\n    将 sample 减半， per-leaf sample size 更小 → CM correction 的 M⁻¹ operation 放大了 leaf-level\n    estimation noise → subgroup aggregation 时 noise 不 cancel 而 compound。 K=4/extreme\n    最严重因为 4 个子群中 sg0 (lowest error) 被 global CM 过度校正， 且 forest 的 nonlinear estimation\n    使得 over-correction 的 propagation 是 multiplicative 而非 additive。ec_hte_forest 的\n    mean |bias| 0.061 (vs global 0.107) 代表 ~2.6x bias reduction (落在 best 档 [2.0, 4.5])。RMSE\n    0.229 > global 0.166 体现了 bias-RMSE tradeoff (per-subgroup CM estimation variance\n    在 forest 上更大)， 这是 Writing Requirement #11 要求 disclose 的。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - title: CausalForest Method Comparison (mean across 8 configs)\n    columns:\n    - method\n    - mean_abs_bias\n    - mean_rmse\n    - debiasing_hurts_cases\n    rows:\n    - - naive_forest\n      - 0.156\n      - 0.178\n      - —\n    - - global_forest\n      - 0.107\n      - 0.166\n      - 9\n    - - ec_hte_forest\n      - 0.061\n      - 0.229\n      - 0\n  - title: Debiasing Hurts — CausalForest vs DIM\n    columns:\n    - estimator\n    - K\n    - max_ratio\n    - worst_config\n    - mechanism\n    rows:\n    - - DIM\n      - 2\n      - 2.86\n      - extreme/sg0\n      - additive over-correction\n    - - DIM\n      - 4\n      - 2.41\n      - extreme/sg0\n      - distributed over-correction\n    - - CausalForest\n      - 2\n      - 3.2\n      - extreme/sg0\n      - multiplicative via leaves\n    - - CausalForest\n      - 4\n      - 5.9\n      - extreme/sg0\n      - compounding leaf noise\n  - title: K=2, n_expert=500 — Near-Zero Bias Detail\n    columns:\n    - config\n    - ec_hte_bias\n    - global_bias\n    - naive_bias\n    - reduction_factor\n    rows:\n    - - extreme/sg0\n      - 0.004\n      - 0.109\n      - 0.052\n      - 27.3\n    - - extreme/sg1\n      - 0.013\n      - 0.033\n      - 0.085\n      - 2.5\n    - - moderate/sg0\n      - 0.008\n      - 0.045\n      - 0.028\n      - 5.6\n    - - moderate/sg1\n      - 0.011\n      - 0.022\n      - 0.065\n      - 2.0\n  figures_description:\n  - DIM vs CausalForest debiasing-hurts amplification comparison (grouped bar chart)\n  - ec_hte_forest bias across n_expert, showing convergence to near-zero\n  analysis: 'CausalForest integration 是 Claim 2 的 critical evidence：paper claims \"CausalForestDML\"\n    但仅有 DIM results 会被审稿人视为 claim-evidence gap。5.9x amplification strengthens Claim\n    1 (\"debiasing can hurt even more with nonlinear estimators\")。 bias-RMSE tradeoff\n    (ec_hte RMSE 38% higher than global) 必须在 paper 中 诚实讨论——defense: (1) bias 是 primary\n    metric for policy decisions， (2) RMSE 在 n≥500 时 competitive，(3) coverage 仍然 near-nominal。'\n","numLines":1290,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1290}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_017DxSEWa4dhv21bzC71VMty","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me now carefully review this paper and prepare the review report. I've read both the PDF and the experiment design context. Let me now dispatch a thorough review.\n\nLet me analyze the paper systematically:\n\n**Title**: \"When Debiasing Backfires: Heterogeneous Misclassification Bias in LLM-Annotated Treatment Effect Estimation\"\n\n**Summary**: The paper identifies that applying global (pooled) confusion-matrix correction to subgroup-level CATE estimates introduces systematic bias proportional to Δπ × Δτ (product of misclassification heterogeneity and CATE heterogeneity). \n\nThe authors propose EC-HTE, a hierarchical Bayesian approach that performs correction at the subgroup level rather than globally, and they introduce a diagnostic criterion based on cross-validation AUC to assess when this matters. They validate their approach across synthetic, semi-synthetic, and real datasets including TweetEval and UC Berkeley hate speech data, and show it integrates well with CausalForest.\n\nNow assessing against EMNLP 2026 standards.\n\n**Strengths:**\n1. Well-defined problem with clear practical relevance - LLMs are widely used for annotation in CSS, and the bias mechanism identified is non-obvious\n2. Strong theoretical contribution - exact bias decomposition identity (Theorem 1), not just a bound\n3. Comprehensive experimental validation spanning 3,600 Monte Carlo runs across multiple data regimes and integration with causal forest methods\n4. Honest reporting of boundary conditions and tradeoffs, with real data framed appropriately as pattern consistency rather than ground truth\n5. Practical diagnostic criterion with cross-validation evaluation\n6. Multi-LLM analysis demonstrating the structural nature of heterogeneity\n7. PPCI composition shows genuine complementarity between approaches\n\n**Weaknesses:**\n1. Theorem 1's presentation lacks precision - the bias decomposition is stated as a function of annotation rate and effect heterogeneity differences, but the exact form only holds for K=2 cases while the general case remains somewhat informal\n\n.\n\n2. The diagnostic criterion achieves CV AUC of 0.78, which is moderate at best, and the leave-one-setting-out evaluation uses only 24 settings with 72 subgroup observations - a small sample that raises questions about generalization beyond these specific configurations.\n\n3. The real data case study shows EC-HTE doesn't actually outperform global correction, and while the paper acknowledges this honestly, it undermines the practical value proposition; the CATE estimates have wide confidence intervals that make it difficult to draw firm conclusions.\n\n4. The non-differential misclassification assumption for LLMs is quite stringent and may not hold in practice.\n\n5. LLM errors likely correlate with outcomes and treatments, which the limitations mention but don't thoroughly investigate for robustness.\n\n6. Expert labels are treated as noise-free, which is unrealistic for many content screening tasks.\n\n7. Scalability becomes problematic with many subgroups - K=8 requires n=1500 for crossover effects, and moderate heterogeneity never crosses over, suggesting the practical utility is limited to K=2-4 with extreme heterogeneity and n≥250.\n\n8. The evaluation focuses on TweetEval sentiment and UC Berkeley hate speech, both standard tasks, without demonstrating generalization to other domains like political stance or moral foundations.\n\n9. The baseline comparisons are narrow, testing only DSL per-subgroup as a non-trivial alternative rather than exploring other Bayesian approaches to measurement error correction.\n\nNow I'm checking which experiments are covered in the paper sections and tables.\n\nAll 11 experiments are accounted for across the main sections and appendices. For the soundness assessment, the theoretical framework is generally solid though Theorem 1 could be more precise in its general form, and the experimental methodology is rigorous with proper Monte Carlo replication and cross-validation.\n\nThe excitement factor sits at a moderate level—while the counterintuitive finding that debiasing can actually harm performance is genuinely surprising and has practical value, the proposed solution relies on established Bayesian methods like Dirichlet priors and partial pooling applied to this new context, which feels somewhat incremental. The diagnostic criterion adds utility but the moderate AUC values limit its broader impact.\n\nOn reproducibility, the experiments are well-documented with clear specifications for sample sizes, number of regimes, and Monte Carlo runs, and the synthetic data generation is fully transparent. The semi-synthetic experiments use publicly available TweetEval data and the real data comes from the UC Berkeley corpus, with MCMC diagnostics properly reported. The main gaps are that code availability isn't mentioned and reproducing the GPT-4.1 annotations would require direct API access.\n\nReconsidering the overall contribution—the paper identifies a previously overlooked bias mechanism, derives an exact identity, proposes a practical correction framework with a diagnostic criterion, and demonstrates composition with existing methods. Combined with the experimental rigor (11 experiments, 3,600 Monte Carlo runs, multiple estimators and LLMs tested), this feels like a more complete package than initially assessed. The writing is clear and the authors are transparent about limitations, which strengthens the work for a venue like EMNLP.\n\nThat said, the Bayesian techniques themselves aren't novel—the real value lies in problem identification and formalization rather than methodological innovation. A score of 3.5 seems right: it's a solid contribution with meaningful insights, but the limited technical novelty may keep it from reaching the excitement threshold for the main conference.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":30023,"cache_read_input_tokens":23661,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":30023},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"33779107-04cc-4691-9d8a-87f3f46280c6","uuid":"2afb6fd0-87e0-435b-a1fa-8cbd28a9d7ad"}
